{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"aae8393d6dfae1c25","tool_use_id":"toolu_01MfkKFXD452moGhCNT59ipP","description":"Writing /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/impl-rationale.md","subagent_type":"Implementer","usage":{"total_tokens":67544,"tool_uses":33,"duration_ms":152515},"last_tool_name":"Write","uuid":"9461befb-79c2-40c8-b919-a9d160a529fc","session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01TXCpimxSc4ZMfg31ktkAgH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BuJRgarAE7uEmSjxnY6NDq","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/impl-rationale.md","content":"# impl-rationale.md — The Dawning Archaic (sos_1)\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### Class hierarchy\n`TheDawningArchaic` extends `Creature` directly (not `CardImpl`) because the card spec says it's a \"Legendary Creature — Avatar\". All creature-specific fields (`base_power`, `base_toughness`, `summoning_sick`, combat flags, etc.) are provided by `Creature.__init__` via `kwargs.setdefault` pattern used consistently throughout FDN reference implementations.\n\n### Static properties\nAll static properties are set via `kwargs.setdefault(...)` in `__init__` so that callers can still override them (e.g., for testing). This follows the FDN reference card pattern exactly.\n\n### Cost reduction (`cost_reduction()`)\nThe `cost_reduction()` hook is already wired into the casting pipeline via `get_cost_reduction()` in `engine/casting.py`. We count instants and sorceries in the controller's graveyard using `CardType.INSTANT` and `CardType.SORCERY` membership checks. The result is capped at the card's generic mana component (10) so the returned value is never more than the card's total generic cost, preventing negative costs (the engine's `get_cost_reduction` also clamps, but we cap early to be explicit about the rule).\n\n### Attack trigger registration\n`register_triggers()` registers a single `TriggerRegistration` for `AttacksTriggeredEvent`. The `condition` lambda uses `event.creature is source` (identity check) so the trigger only fires when this specific card attacks. The `controller` field is captured from `self.controller` at registration time, matching the engine's APNAP ordering requirement.\n\n### Free-cast trigger effect\nRather than using `cast_spell_free()` (which calls `_resolve_spell()` and would send the spell to the graveyard on resolution), the effect directly:\n1. Moves the target instant/sorcery from graveyard to the controller's stack zone\n2. Pushes a custom `StackObject` whose `on_resolve` callback calls `spell.on_resolve(game)` and then sends the spell to exile\n\nThis approach avoids the engine's normal `_resolve_spell` post-resolution zone-move, allowing the explicit exile destination. It correctly handles the case where the resolved spell has no effect of its own (the `on_resolve` default is a no-op in `CardImpl`).\n\n### Exile placement\nThe custom `_free_cast_resolve` removes the spell from the stack zone, calls `spell.on_resolve(game)` for its effect, then places it in `owner.zones[Zone.EXILE]`. For non-permanent cards (instants/sorceries), this is always the correct destination per the card's oracle text. Permanent-type spells (if any were mistakenly cast this way) are sent to the battlefield as a safety fallback.\n\n### No persistent replacement effects\nThe exile redirect is implemented inline in the custom StackObject rather than as a persistent `ReplacementEffect` registered on the card. This is correct because:\n- The replacement only applies to spells cast via the trigger, not to all zone transitions\n- A `ReplacementEffect` for `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` from the stack would not fire anyway (since `move_to_zone` only checks replacements when leaving the battlefield, not from the stack)\n\n## Deviations from card spec's mental model\nThe oracle text says \"If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead,\" which reads like a replacement effect. However, since `_resolve_spell` in `casting.py` calls `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.GRAVEYARD)` directly (without a replacement event parameter), a `ReplacementEffect` registered on the engine's `ReplacementManager` would not intercept this. The custom StackObject approach sidesteps this limitation cleanly.\n\n## Conventions established\n- Free-cast from graveyard with exile redirect: use a custom StackObject with an inline `on_resolve` that explicitly routes to exile, rather than relying on replacement effects (which the engine doesn't support for STACK→GRAVEYARD transitions).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1730,"cache_read_input_tokens":64701,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1730,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":45,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MfkKFXD452moGhCNT59ipP","session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"7b37680a-b06d-47d1-8668-49dc49c24ab6","request_id":"req_011CbTyeMdNdmoQCAzS6Lxqb","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implementer for sos_1"}
