{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01WjrRDkq5fNEpijFuocxznQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HTid4632wrbAmqKsNhGfc3","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/review.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":875,"cache_read_input_tokens":8533,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":875,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01A34n7tFhobSMjjakbUA9Uq","session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"1632259a-756e-45c3-838b-cb5a87b7ce84","request_id":"req_011CbTypPndLeGU4bVGZ9q8T","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revision round for sos_1"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HTid4632wrbAmqKsNhGfc3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n4\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py\",\n5\t    \"line\": 96,\n6\t    \"comment\": \"The _attack_trigger_effect function reimplements free-cast logic that already exists in engine.casting.cast_spell_free(). The implementation manually moves the card from graveyard to stack zone, builds a StackObject with a custom on_resolve closure, and calls spell.on_resolve() directly — bypassing the engine's resolution pipeline (_resolve_spell). This means: (1) card.get_targets() is never called so targeted spells never target anything, (2) card.on_cast() hook is never invoked, (3) card.chosen_targets is never set before on_resolve is called (breaking any spell that reads self.chosen_targets). The correct approach is to call cast_spell_free(game, controller, spell, Zone.GRAVEYARD) to place the spell on the stack through the proper pipeline, then handle the exile replacement via a replacement effect or a custom on_resolve wrapper that delegates to the engine's _resolve_spell output.\"\n7\t  },\n8\t  {\n9\t    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n10\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py\",\n11\t    \"line\": 101,\n12\t    \"comment\": \"The attack trigger fires on the first instant/sorcery found in the graveyard with no player interaction. The oracle text says 'you MAY cast TARGET instant or sorcery card'. Both the 'may' (player can decline) and 'target' (player picks which card) are unimplemented. Without a player choice (choose_yes_no for 'may', choose_target for selecting which card), the ability is mandatory and non-deterministic (it picks the first card in iteration order). Per MTG rules 601.2 and 114, a targeted ability requires the controller to choose a target at announcement time.\"\n13\t  },\n14\t  {\n15\t    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n16\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py\",\n17\t    \"line\": 156,\n18\t    \"comment\": \"The exile-instead-of-graveyard replacement is implemented by calling spell.on_resolve(g) inside a hand-rolled _free_cast_resolve callback, then unconditionally adding the spell to exile. This does not compose correctly with the engine: (1) if the spell itself moves to the graveyard inside on_resolve() (e.g. by calling move_to_zone()), it will be double-placed because the outer closure also does owner.zones[Zone.EXILE].add(spell); (2) the approach does not go through the replacement effect manager, so any other replacement effects that apply to that spell going to a zone are silently skipped; (3) the battlefield branch adds the card directly via ZoneContainer.add() rather than through move_to_zone(), skipping ETB trigger registration, EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent, and register_triggers/register_replacement_effects calls for any permanent the spell might resolve into.\"\n19\t  },\n20\t  {\n21\t    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n22\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py\",\n23\t    \"line\": 19,\n24\t    \"comment\": \"ReplacementEffect is imported but never used in the module. The comment in register_replacement_effects mentions that the free-cast exile replacement is 'registered transiently' but in practice no ReplacementEffect is registered at all. The unused import should be removed to avoid confusion.\"\n25\t  }\n26\t]\n27\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01A34n7tFhobSMjjakbUA9Uq","session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"737f4a16-f9df-49f0-ad8c-c979825345e8","timestamp":"2026-05-27T23:58:10.235Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revision round for sos_1"}
