{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A34n7tFhobSMjjakbUA9Uq","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All files are in place. \n\nREVISION_DONE\ndisagreement_count: 1\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/impl-revised.diff\ndisagreements_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/disagreements.json\n\n**Summary of changes:**\n\n- **Strict comment #1 (applied):** Replaced manual `StackObject` construction with `cast_spell_free(game, controller, spell, Zone.GRAVEYARD)` — the spell now goes through the proper casting pipeline (targeting, `on_cast`, `chosen_targets`).\n\n- **Strict comment #3 (applied):** The exile-instead-of-graveyard behavior is now implemented by wrapping `stack_obj.on_resolve` after `cast_spell_free` returns. The wrapper calls the original `_resolve_spell`-based callback, then checks if the spell landed in the graveyard and moves it to exile. This avoids double-placement and correctly handles both permanent and non-permanent spells.\n\n- **Strict comment #2 (partial disagreement):** `choose_yes_no` and `choose_card` calls are now present for \"may\" and target selection, but wrapped in `try/except` with fallbacks. Unconditional calls would break all attack trigger tests because the tests use `DeterministicPlayer` with an empty script queue — calling `choose_yes_no` on such a player raises `ScriptExhaustedError`. The tests define the contract and cannot be modified per workspace rules."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a2c1f2490a2280dfc (use SendMessage with to: 'a2c1f2490a2280dfc' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 62661\ntool_uses: 35\nduration_ms: 209180</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"948f3b2f-d8b1-48bb-881a-49be1bd1dc06","timestamp":"2026-05-28T00:01:35.680Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Revise the implementation of card sos_1 to address strict review comments.\n\nCard ID: sos_1\nCard spec: /workspace/car