{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01W78Bb2dgikkqMyekJUNfvh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01C9gsDHyyrSH72cvPiZgnWe","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_4/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale for SOS 4 — Together as One\n\n## File: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py`\n\nTogether as One is a Converge Sorcery ({6}) that produces three simultaneous\neffects scaled by X = the number of colors of mana spent to cast it:\n1. Target player draws X cards.\n2. The spell deals X damage to any target (player or creature).\n3. The casting player gains X life.\n\nThe implementation pattern follows FDN 205 (Wardens of the Cycle): the cast\npipeline records the number of distinct colors paid into `card.colors_spent`\n(an int), and `on_resolve` reads that integer to drive the effects.  Tests set\n`colors_spent` directly to decouple them from the full cast pipeline, exactly\nas the FDN reference tests do.\n\n---\n\n### `TestTogetherAsOneProperties` (4 tests)\n\n- `test_is_sorcery` — The card must subclass `Sorcery` (not `Instant` or\n  `Creature`).\n- `test_name` — Card name must be \"Together as One\" per the spec.\n- `test_mana_cost` — Mana cost must parse as `{6}` (colorless generic).\n- `test_card_type_is_sorcery` — `CardType.SORCERY` must be in `card_types`.\n\n---\n\n### `TestTogetherAsOneConvergeAttribute` (2 tests)\n\n- `test_colors_spent_defaults_to_zero` — Like Wardens of the Cycle, the\n  attribute must exist and default to 0 before any cast pipeline runs.\n- `test_colors_spent_is_integer` — Must be an `int` (not None or a list)\n  so arithmetic in `on_resolve` works without a type check.\n\n---\n\n### `TestTogetherAsOneZeroConverge` (4 tests)\n\nWhen `colors_spent == 0`, X = 0, so all three effects are no-ops:\n\n- `test_zero_colors_does_not_raise` — Baseline: resolution must not raise.\n- `test_zero_colors_no_life_change` — Casting player gains 0 life.\n- `test_zero_colors_no_draw` — Draw target draws 0 cards.\n- `test_zero_colors_no_damage` — Damage target loses 0 life.\n\nEdge case coverage: X = 0 is the most common failure mode for converge cards\n(forgetting to guard the loop / arithmetic against zero).\n\n---\n\n### `TestTogetherAsOneDrawEffect` (4 tests)\n\nVerifies that the draw target player's hand grows by exactly X:\n\n- `test_one_color_target_draws_one_card` — X = 1.\n- `test_two_colors_target_draws_two_cards` — X = 2.\n- `test_three_colors_target_draws_three_cards` — X = 3.\n- `test_casting_player_can_also_be_draw_target` — Oracle text says \"target\n  player\", which includes the caster themselves.\n\nLibrary cards are seeded via `ZoneContainer.add` so that draws actually move\na card; we assert on hand size delta.\n\n---\n\n### `TestTogetherAsOneDamageEffect` (4 tests)\n\nVerifies that X damage is dealt to the chosen damage target:\n\n- `test_one_color_deals_one_damage_to_player` — Player life decreases by 1.\n- `test_three_colors_deals_three_damage_to_player` — Player life decreases by 3.\n- `test_damage_to_creature_marks_damage` — Oracle says \"any target\", so\n  creatures are legal; `damage_marked` must increase by X.\n- `test_five_colors_deals_five_damage_to_creature` — Max colors (X = 5).\n\nCreature damage tests also verify the \"any target\" language — the damage\ntarget is separate from the draw target.\n\n---\n\n### `TestTogetherAsOneLifeGain` (3 tests)\n\nVerifies that the casting player gains exactly X life:\n\n- `test_one_color_gains_one_life` — X = 1.\n- `test_three_colors_gains_three_life` — X = 3.\n- `test_five_colors_gains_five_life` — X = 5 (maximum converge value).\n\n---\n\n### `TestTogetherAsOneAllEffects` (1 test)\n\n- `test_two_colors_all_three_effects` — Integration: with X = 2, all three\n  effects fire and their magnitudes are checked in a single resolution.  This\n  guards against an implementation that accidentally applies only one or two\n  of the three effects.\n\n---\n\n### `TestTogetherAsOneTargeting` (3 tests)\n\n- `test_get_targets_returns_list` — The return value of `get_targets` must\n  be a list (not None or a TargetRequirement directly).\n- `test_get_targets_returns_two_requirements` — Two distinct target slots:\n  one for \"target player\" (draw), one for \"any target\" (damage).\n- `test_no_chosen_targets_does_not_raise` — If `chosen_targets` was never\n  set (e.g. the spell was countered mid-resolution or tests don't set it),\n  `on_resolve` must exit cleanly.\n\n---\n\n## Edge cases NOT covered (and why)\n\n- **Converge via cast pipeline** — Testing the full cast pipeline (mana\n  payment tracking through `last_payment_colors`) is covered by the FDN 205\n  Wardens reference tests and the engine test suite.  The card's own tests\n  focus on the `on_resolve` contract given a pre-set `colors_spent`.\n- **Draw from empty library** — The engine's `draw_card` handles the\n  empty-library case by setting `drawn_from_empty_library`; that is engine\n  behavior, not card behavior.\n- **Damage to planeswalker** — The engine's `deal_damage` handles planeswalker\n  loyalty loss; the card just calls `deal_damage(game, self, target, X)` and\n  doesn't need a separate test.\n- **Protection** — Protection preventing damage is engine behavior\n  (`deal_damage` checks `has_protection_from`); out of scope for this card's\n  unit tests.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4597,"cache_read_input_tokens":58089,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4597,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016CM3Tv5RBDhHPpeH8C79Ts","session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"195db868-19f3-4835-afaf-faf9128d59a2","request_id":"req_011CbTzHNvHmq8puqT8PHobq","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Tester for sos_4"}
