{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GGUftrRhtgASZGpqMiosec","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation Rationale: sos_4 — Together as One\n2\t\n3\t## Design Decisions\n4\t\n5\t### Base class: `Sorcery`\n6\tThe card is a Sorcery type (type line \"Sorcery\"), so `Sorcery` from `engine.card` is the correct base class. It automatically adds `CardType.SORCERY` to `card_types`.\n7\t\n8\t### Converge pattern: `colors_spent` attribute\n9\tFollowed the exact same pattern as FDN 205 (Wardens of the Cycle), which uses a `self.colors_spent: int = 0` instance attribute initialized to 0. This attribute is set externally by the cast pipeline or directly by test code.\n10\t\n11\t### `get_targets` returns two entries\n12\tThe tests assert `len(get_targets(game)) == 2`. The first entry is the \"draw target\" (a player) and the second is the \"damage target\" (any target — player or creature). Each entry is a descriptive dict with `description` and `zone` keys, consistent with the minimal shape other cards use.\n13\t\n14\t### `on_resolve` logic\n15\tThree simultaneous effects driven by `colors_spent` (X):\n16\t1. `chosen_targets[0]` draws X cards via `engine.game.draw_card`.\n17\t2. `chosen_targets[1]` takes X damage via `engine.game.deal_damage`.\n18\t3. `self.controller` gains X life via direct `controller.life += x` (same pattern as fdn_58, fdn_137, etc.) plus firing `GainsLifeTriggeredEvent` for completeness.\n19\t\n20\tWhen `x == 0` the method returns immediately (no-op). When `chosen_targets` is absent or too short the code safely skips the missing effects (no raise), satisfying the `test_no_chosen_targets_does_not_raise` test.\n21\t\n22\t### Guard for draw target\n23\tDraw target is guarded with `hasattr(draw_target, \"zones\")` to distinguish players (who have a zones dict) from creatures; this prevents accidentally drawing for a creature target if the order is swapped, and is consistent with how FDN cards check player-ness.\n24\t\n25\t## Conventions Established\n26\t- Converge cards store the distinct-colors count in `self.colors_spent: int = 0`, set externally (same as fdn_205).\n27\t- `get_targets()` for multi-target spells returns a list of dicts with `description`/`zone` keys.\n28\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"fce42cad-2393-4cae-aca0-6214591df00e","timestamp":"2026-05-28T00:09:42.235Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_4/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation Rationale: sos_4 — Together as One\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### Base class: `Sorcery`\nThe card is a Sorcery type (type line \"Sorcery\"), so `Sorcery` from `engine.card` is the correct base class. It automatically adds `CardType.SORCERY` to `card_types`.\n\n### Converge pattern: `colors_spent` attribute\nFollowed the exact same pattern as FDN 205 (Wardens of the Cycle), which uses a `self.colors_spent: int = 0` instance attribute initialized to 0. This attribute is set externally by the cast pipeline or directly by test code.\n\n### `get_targets` returns two entries\nThe tests assert `len(get_targets(game)) == 2`. The first entry is the \"draw target\" (a player) and the second is the \"damage target\" (any target — player or creature). Each entry is a descriptive dict with `description` and `zone` keys, consistent with the minimal shape other cards use.\n\n### `on_resolve` logic\nThree simultaneous effects driven by `colors_spent` (X):\n1. `chosen_targets[0]` draws X cards via `engine.game.draw_card`.\n2. `chosen_targets[1]` takes X damage via `engine.game.deal_damage`.\n3. `self.controller` gains X life via direct `controller.life += x` (same pattern as fdn_58, fdn_137, etc.) plus firing `GainsLifeTriggeredEvent` for completeness.\n\nWhen `x == 0` the method returns immediately (no-op). When `chosen_targets` is absent or too short the code safely skips the missing effects (no raise), satisfying the `test_no_chosen_targets_does_not_raise` test.\n\n### Guard for draw target\nDraw target is guarded with `hasattr(draw_target, \"zones\")` to distinguish players (who have a zones dict) from creatures; this prevents accidentally drawing for a creature target if the order is swapped, and is consistent with how FDN cards check player-ness.\n\n## Conventions Established\n- Converge cards store the distinct-colors count in `self.colors_spent: int = 0`, set externally (same as fdn_205).\n- `get_targets()` for multi-target spells returns a list of dicts with `description`/`zone` keys.\n","numLines":28,"startLine":1,"totalLines":28}}}
