{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011GWogJMeX9nabGUcyHhPcp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Revision Rationale for sos_57 (Mana Sculpt)\n2\t\n3\t## Strict Comments Applied\n4\t\n5\t### 1. BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent at POSTCOMBAT_MAIN (engine/turn.py)\n6\t\n7\tThe original implementation only fired `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` at `(Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN, None)`. The oracle text says \"at the beginning of your **next** main phase,\" which may well be postcombat main — for instance, if Mana Sculpt is cast during precombat main, the *next* main phase is postcombat main.\n8\t\n9\tFix: changed the `elif current == (Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN, None):` branch to `elif current in ((Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN, None), (Phase.POSTCOMBAT_MAIN, None)):`. The event fires for both main phases. The condition closure in Mana Sculpt's trigger already filters on `event.player is controller`, so it only reacts to the right player's main phase. Because it's a one-shot trigger (unregisters on first fire), it will fire at whichever comes next after resolution, which is the correct behavior.\n10\t\n11\t### 2. Mana amount uses actual mana_spent when available (cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py)\n12\t\n13\tThe original code used `mana_cost.cmc` which treats X as 0. For a spell like `{X}{R}` cast for X=5, CMC would give 1, not 6.\n14\t\n15\tFix: `on_resolve` now first checks `getattr(target, \"mana_spent\", None)` on the `StackObject`. If the engine sets that attribute (e.g., when casting with X), it uses that value instead. If `mana_spent` is absent (as in the current StackObject implementation and all test helpers), it falls back to `mana_cost.cmc`. This is a forward-compatible fix: all existing tests continue to pass (they use non-X spells), and future engine support for recording `mana_spent` on StackObjects will automatically produce correct results for X-cost spells.\n16\t\n17\t## Advisory Comments\n18\t\n19\tTwo advisory comments (SLF001 private access to `game.stack._items` and the `can_cast` LAND exclusion logic) were acknowledged but not changed, as there is no public removal API on the Stack class and the filtering logic is functionally correct for all practical cases.\n20\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"f551312c-f316-44ad-b205-6dee62660e65","timestamp":"2026-05-28T00:34:38.323Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/impl-revised-rationale.md","content":"# Revision Rationale for sos_57 (Mana Sculpt)\n\n## Strict Comments Applied\n\n### 1. BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent at POSTCOMBAT_MAIN (engine/turn.py)\n\nThe original implementation only fired `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` at `(Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN, None)`. The oracle text says \"at the beginning of your **next** main phase,\" which may well be postcombat main — for instance, if Mana Sculpt is cast during precombat main, the *next* main phase is postcombat main.\n\nFix: changed the `elif current == (Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN, None):` branch to `elif current in ((Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN, None), (Phase.POSTCOMBAT_MAIN, None)):`. The event fires for both main phases. The condition closure in Mana Sculpt's trigger already filters on `event.player is controller`, so it only reacts to the right player's main phase. Because it's a one-shot trigger (unregisters on first fire), it will fire at whichever comes next after resolution, which is the correct behavior.\n\n### 2. Mana amount uses actual mana_spent when available (cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py)\n\nThe original code used `mana_cost.cmc` which treats X as 0. For a spell like `{X}{R}` cast for X=5, CMC would give 1, not 6.\n\nFix: `on_resolve` now first checks `getattr(target, \"mana_spent\", None)` on the `StackObject`. If the engine sets that attribute (e.g., when casting with X), it uses that value instead. If `mana_spent` is absent (as in the current StackObject implementation and all test helpers), it falls back to `mana_cost.cmc`. This is a forward-compatible fix: all existing tests continue to pass (they use non-X spells), and future engine support for recording `mana_spent` on StackObjects will automatically produce correct results for X-cost spells.\n\n## Advisory Comments\n\nTwo advisory comments (SLF001 private access to `game.stack._items` and the `can_cast` LAND exclusion logic) were acknowledged but not changed, as there is no public removal API on the Stack class and the filtering logic is functionally correct for all practical cases.\n","numLines":20,"startLine":1,"totalLines":20}}}
