{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01Uzv8hrsMTQoiWbeBBMtrLp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HQmLrLq33Qcs4CJtq3Pkvy","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/coordinator-directives.md","content":"# Coordinator Directives for sos_97\n\n## Untestable item 1: Target filtering for −2 ability (CMC ≤ 3)\nThe Implementer should expose target requirements for loyalty abilities in a way that tests can verify. Either:\n- Add a `get_loyalty_ability_targets(ability_index)` method, or\n- Include a `filter_fn` attribute on TargetRequirement objects that the tests can call directly.\nThis allows tests to verify that CMC > 3 creatures are rejected without requiring full game target validation.\n\n## Untestable item 2: Coin flip randomness for −7 ability\nThe Implementer should add a coin_flip() helper (or use an injectable randomness hook) so tests can control coin flip results. Options:\n- Add a `_coin_flip_results` attribute on the card or game that, when set, overrides random results\n- Or accept a `coin_flip_fn` parameter defaulting to `lambda: random.random() < 0.5`\n- The `skipped_turns` for the opponent should be tracked in a way tests can observe (e.g., via a counter on the Player or game state).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":528,"cache_read_input_tokens":43147,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":528},"output_tokens":27,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"ddc9147d-4045-43c5-9d67-4fa3c0fc4ce5","request_id":"req_011CbU2vjbm3Y4V9VAojAhRm"}
