{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018UgMQMeuazQNU8zYdYw49G","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator Directives for sos_97\n2\t\n3\t## Untestable item 1: Target filtering for −2 ability (CMC ≤ 3)\n4\tThe Implementer should expose target requirements for loyalty abilities in a way that tests can verify. Either:\n5\t- Add a `get_loyalty_ability_targets(ability_index)` method, or\n6\t- Include a `filter_fn` attribute on TargetRequirement objects that the tests can call directly.\n7\tThis allows tests to verify that CMC > 3 creatures are rejected without requiring full game target validation.\n8\t\n9\t## Untestable item 2: Coin flip randomness for −7 ability\n10\tThe Implementer should add a coin_flip() helper (or use an injectable randomness hook) so tests can control coin flip results. Options:\n11\t- Add a `_coin_flip_results` attribute on the card or game that, when set, overrides random results\n12\t- Or accept a `coin_flip_fn` parameter defaulting to `lambda: random.random() < 0.5`\n13\t- The `skipped_turns` for the opponent should be tracked in a way tests can observe (e.g., via a counter on the Player or game state).\n14\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01SABz7nzXit2cwxxwgaVRMd","session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"5f7f776b-0f42-4754-88ab-a9b3f3a2c307","timestamp":"2026-05-28T00:39:18.215Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implementer for sos_97"}
