{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01L9nEjyBZLEShy8HkeN25xN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01S73MALAS3oFJz7TweaWBMt","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation Rationale for SOS 97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### Class Hierarchy\nExtends `Planeswalker` from `engine.card`, which provides `starting_loyalty`, `loyalty`, and the `get_loyalty_abilities()` override point. Sets `Supertype.LEGENDARY` and subtype `\"Ral\"` in `__init__`.\n\n### Four Loyalty Abilities\nThe card spec defines four loyalty abilities (+1, −1, −2, −7). I return all four from `get_loyalty_abilities()`. This correctly satisfies tests for `test_fourth_ability_cost_minus_seven` and the `TestRalZarekUltimate` class, which all require the −7 ability to exist.\n\n**Test contradiction (1 failing test):** `test_returns_list_of_three` asserts `len(abilities) == 3`, but `test_minus_two_ability_cost` asserts `abilities[2].loyalty_cost == -2` and `test_fourth_ability_cost_minus_seven` asserts `-7 in costs`. These three tests are mutually exclusive — a list of 3 cannot contain both -2 at index 2 and -7 somewhere in the list. Returning 4 abilities maximizes passing tests (29/30) versus returning 3 (which would fail both `test_fourth_ability_cost_minus_seven` and all 4 `TestRalZarekUltimate` tests = 5 failing).\n\n### +1 Surveil 2\n- Takes the top 2 cards from the library (using `library.top(n)` then removes them).\n- For each card (topmost first), calls `controller.choose_yes_no()` to decide graveyard vs. keep.\n- Kept cards go back to the top in their original order.\n- Wrapped in try/except per KEY_DECISIONS convention for DeterministicPlayer compatibility.\n\n### −1 Discard\n- Reads `ral._resolve_targets` (a list of player objects, set by the test or game engine).\n- For each targeted player, calls `player.choose_card()` (with try/except fallback).\n- Directly removes from hand and adds to graveyard (no `move_to_zone` needed; discard is simple).\n\n### −2 Graveyard Return\n- Reads `ral._resolve_target` for the creature.\n- Searches all players' graveyards for the target (to handle the case where the owner may differ from controller).\n- Uses `move_to_zone(game, target, Zone.GRAVEYARD, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)` for proper ETB trigger firing.\n\n### −7 Coin Flip Turn Skip\n- Injectable `_coin_flip_results` attribute (list of bools) overrides `random.random()` for deterministic testing.\n- Counts heads; if zero, returns early (no-op).\n- Simulates \"opponent skips X turns\" by granting X extra turns to the controller via `game.extra_turns`. This matches the engine's extra_turns model and how the tests verify the outcome.\n\n### Target State\n- `_resolve_targets`: list of players (for −1)\n- `_resolve_target`: single object (for −2 and −7)\n- `_coin_flip_results`: injectable coin flip sequence (for −7)\nAll initialized in `__init__` for clean state.\n\n## Conventions Established\n- Planeswalker ability state stored as `_resolve_target` / `_resolve_targets` on the card instance (matches pattern from FDN planeswalkers like `ChandraFlameshaper`).\n- Coin flip injection via `_coin_flip_results` list attribute as directed by coordinator directives.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":87,"cache_read_input_tokens":58748,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":87,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":46,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01SABz7nzXit2cwxxwgaVRMd","session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"5020b16e-41ba-4fd0-af2e-54142a36ea0c","request_id":"req_011CbU37VVzTt3wpK98NDRef","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implementer for sos_97"}
