{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A2cZuhzibkk3fVK6S3J4mN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test Dispute for SOS 97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer\n2\t\n3\t## Disputed Test\n4\t\n5\t**Test:** `TestRalZarekLoyaltyAbilities::test_returns_list_of_three`\n6\t**File:** `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py`, line 64\n7\t**Assertion:** `assert len(abilities) == 3`\n8\t\n9\t## Why This Test Is Wrong\n10\t\n11\tThe card spec for SOS 97 (Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer) defines **four** loyalty abilities:\n12\t1. +1: Surveil 2\n13\t2. −1: Any number of target players each discard a card\n14\t3. −2: Return target creature card with MV ≤ 3 from graveyard to battlefield\n15\t4. −7: Flip five coins; opponent skips X turns\n16\t\n17\tThe test `test_returns_list_of_three` asserts `len(abilities) == 3`, but this directly contradicts two other tests in the same class:\n18\t\n19\t- `test_minus_two_ability_cost` asserts `abilities[2].loyalty_cost == -2` (so index 2 is the −2 ability)\n20\t- `test_fourth_ability_cost_minus_seven` asserts `-7 in costs` (so −7 must be in the list)\n21\t\n22\tWith exactly 3 items where `abilities[2].loyalty_cost == -2`, the costs would be `[+1, -1, -2]`, which does not contain `-7`. Therefore:\n23\t- It is impossible for `len(abilities) == 3` AND `-7 in costs` AND `abilities[2].loyalty_cost == -2` to all be true simultaneously.\n24\t\n25\t## Correct Behavior\n26\t\n27\t`get_loyalty_abilities()` should return a list of **4** abilities: `[+1, -1, -2, -7]`. This satisfies:\n28\t- `test_plus_one_ability_cost` (abilities[0] = +1)\n29\t- `test_minus_one_ability_cost` (abilities[1] = -1)\n30\t- `test_minus_two_ability_cost` (abilities[2] = -2)\n31\t- `test_fourth_ability_cost_minus_seven` (-7 in costs)\n32\t- All `TestRalZarekUltimate` tests (which find and exercise the −7 ability)\n33\t\n34\tThe test `test_returns_list_of_three` appears to have been written with an incorrect expected count (should be 4) or the test name is misleading. The docstring for `test_fourth_ability_cost_minus_seven` explicitly states \"Card has a −7 ability (coin-flip turn-skip); it must be in the list\" — which is incompatible with a list of 3.\n35\t\n36\t## Implementation Decision\n37\t\n38\tI return 4 abilities to maximize passing tests (29/30). The `test_returns_list_of_three` test fails due to this genuine contradiction.\n39\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"c2612b5e-67e7-4a1a-8460-7630bf533e98","timestamp":"2026-05-28T00:42:15.689Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/test-dispute.md","content":"# Test Dispute for SOS 97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer\n\n## Disputed Test\n\n**Test:** `TestRalZarekLoyaltyAbilities::test_returns_list_of_three`\n**File:** `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py`, line 64\n**Assertion:** `assert len(abilities) == 3`\n\n## Why This Test Is Wrong\n\nThe card spec for SOS 97 (Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer) defines **four** loyalty abilities:\n1. +1: Surveil 2\n2. −1: Any number of target players each discard a card\n3. −2: Return target creature card with MV ≤ 3 from graveyard to battlefield\n4. −7: Flip five coins; opponent skips X turns\n\nThe test `test_returns_list_of_three` asserts `len(abilities) == 3`, but this directly contradicts two other tests in the same class:\n\n- `test_minus_two_ability_cost` asserts `abilities[2].loyalty_cost == -2` (so index 2 is the −2 ability)\n- `test_fourth_ability_cost_minus_seven` asserts `-7 in costs` (so −7 must be in the list)\n\nWith exactly 3 items where `abilities[2].loyalty_cost == -2`, the costs would be `[+1, -1, -2]`, which does not contain `-7`. Therefore:\n- It is impossible for `len(abilities) == 3` AND `-7 in costs` AND `abilities[2].loyalty_cost == -2` to all be true simultaneously.\n\n## Correct Behavior\n\n`get_loyalty_abilities()` should return a list of **4** abilities: `[+1, -1, -2, -7]`. This satisfies:\n- `test_plus_one_ability_cost` (abilities[0] = +1)\n- `test_minus_one_ability_cost` (abilities[1] = -1)\n- `test_minus_two_ability_cost` (abilities[2] = -2)\n- `test_fourth_ability_cost_minus_seven` (-7 in costs)\n- All `TestRalZarekUltimate` tests (which find and exercise the −7 ability)\n\nThe test `test_returns_list_of_three` appears to have been written with an incorrect expected count (should be 4) or the test name is misleading. The docstring for `test_fourth_ability_cost_minus_seven` explicitly states \"Card has a −7 ability (coin-flip turn-skip); it must be in the list\" — which is incompatible with a list of 3.\n\n## Implementation Decision\n\nI return 4 abilities to maximize passing tests (29/30). The `test_returns_list_of_three` test fails due to this genuine contradiction.\n","numLines":39,"startLine":1,"totalLines":39}}}
