{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KtHJEzwvQoXvP49Xh7oAhU","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"922133dd-fe3b-45fd-94e8-ad6861e522a1","timestamp":"2026-05-28T00:42:29.114Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md","oldString":"## Disagreement arbitration: sos_1 (comment index 1)","newString":"## Test dispute: sos_97 — test_returns_list_of_three\n- **Disputed test**: `TestRalZarekLoyaltyAbilities::test_returns_list_of_three` asserts `len(abilities) == 3`\n- **Tester's intent**: Intended to check the number of loyalty abilities\n- **Implementer's objection**: Card spec defines 4 abilities (+1, -1, -2, -7); asserting len==3 directly contradicts `test_fourth_ability_cost_minus_seven` and `test_minus_two_ability_cost` in the same file\n- **Decision**: Side with Implementer. This is a feasibility objection — the test expects impossible behavior (3 items with index 2 = -2 and -7 also in list). Re-invoke Tester to fix the count assertion to 4.\n\n## Disagreement arbitration: sos_1 (comment index 1)","originalFile":"# Run Decisions\n\nDecisions made during this run only. Before the run ends, migrate anything worth preserving into `KEY_DECISIONS.md`.\n\n## Disagreement arbitration: sos_1 (comment index 1)\n- **Issue**: Reviewer wanted unconditional choose_yes_no/choose_card for \"may\" and target selection.\n- **Implementer**: Calls are present but wrapped in try/except fallback because tests use DeterministicPlayer with empty script queue — unconditional calls would raise ScriptExhaustedError.\n- **Decision**: Side with Implementer. The try/except approach is a reasonable compromise. The player-choice calls are present for real game contexts; fallback to auto-yes/first-target is acceptable when no script is provided. Tests define the contract.\n\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":2,"oldLines":6,"newStart":2,"newLines":12,"lines":[" "," Decisions made during this run only. Before the run ends, migrate anything worth preserving into `KEY_DECISIONS.md`."," ","+## Test dispute: sos_97 — test_returns_list_of_three","+- **Disputed test**: `TestRalZarekLoyaltyAbilities::test_returns_list_of_three` asserts `len(abilities) == 3`","+- **Tester's intent**: Intended to check the number of loyalty abilities","+- **Implementer's objection**: Card spec defines 4 abilities (+1, -1, -2, -7); asserting len==3 directly contradicts `test_fourth_ability_cost_minus_seven` and `test_minus_two_ability_cost` in the same file","+- **Decision**: Side with Implementer. This is a feasibility objection — the test expects impossible behavior (3 items with index 2 = -2 and -7 also in list). Re-invoke Tester to fix the count assertion to 4.","+"," ## Disagreement arbitration: sos_1 (comment index 1)"," - **Issue**: Reviewer wanted unconditional choose_yes_no/choose_card for \"may\" and target selection."," - **Implementer**: Calls are present but wrapped in try/except fallback because tests use DeterministicPlayer with empty script queue — unconditional calls would raise ScriptExhaustedError."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
