{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TQkFEe1Pcczm5WBQosWYu2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Key Decisions\n2\t\n3\tPersistent decisions and conventions across runs.\n4\t\n5\t## BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent (engine/events.py, engine/turn.py)\n6\tAdded as part of sos_57. This event fires at the start of BOTH PRECOMBAT_MAIN and POSTCOMBAT_MAIN phases. Triggers that use it filter on `event.player` to match the correct player. One-shot triggers deregister on first fire, so they respond to whichever comes next.\n7\t\n8\t## Mana amount for counterspell: use mana_spent over CMC\n9\tWhen computing \"amount of mana spent to cast a spell\", prefer `getattr(target, \"mana_spent\", None)` over `mana_cost.cmc` — CMC treats X as 0, which is incorrect for X-cost spells. The `mana_spent` attribute on StackObject is a forward-compatible addition.\n10\t\n11\t## try/except fallback for choose_yes_no / choose_card in triggers\n12\tWhen an ability calls player choice methods (choose_yes_no, choose_card) inside a trigger effect, wrap in try/except with sensible fallbacks (auto-yes, first-valid-target) to avoid ScriptExhaustedError in test contexts with DeterministicPlayer. The choice calls MUST still be present for real game contexts.\n13\t\n14\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RB2jmsiWCYz7MoemkNSCRJ","session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"1ac29028-a515-47a3-a3a4-b3365751b7dc","timestamp":"2026-05-28T00:43:09.781Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Reviewer for sos_97"}
