{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"aaad21a25fed1bc39","tool_use_id":"toolu_01AGpdidDchSkthiJvVqN48E","description":"Writing /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/test-rationale.md","subagent_type":"Tester","usage":{"total_tokens":90150,"tool_uses":27,"duration_ms":149796},"last_tool_name":"Write","uuid":"6a48227b-6e79-432a-a47b-ddd61e60cb67","session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01KdtLuo6Wgvg5WZE9f8hCWj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012XEUHwbR2bNDprCU4vWe8U","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale — SOS 120: Improvisation Capstone\n\n## Card Summary\n\n**Improvisation Capstone** — {5}{R}{R} — Sorcery — Lesson\n\n> Exile cards from the top of your library until you exile cards with total mana value 4 or greater. You may cast any number of spells from among them without paying their mana costs.\n> Paradigm (Then exile this spell. After you first resolve a spell with this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the beginning of each of your first main phases.)\n\n---\n\n## Test File: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py`\n\n### Class: `TestImprovisationCapstoneProperties` (5 tests)\n\n| Test | Requirement |\n|------|-------------|\n| `test_is_sorcery` | Card must be a `Sorcery` subclass |\n| `test_name` | Card name must be `\"Improvisation Capstone\"` |\n| `test_mana_cost` | Mana cost must be `{5}{R}{R}` |\n| `test_sorcery_card_type` | `CardType.SORCERY` must be in `card_types` |\n| `test_lesson_subtype` | `\"Lesson\"` must be in `subtypes` per type line |\n\n---\n\n### Class: `TestImprovisationCapstoneExileEffect` (7 tests)\n\nTests the main resolution effect: *\"Exile cards from the top of your library until you exile cards with total mana value 4 or greater.\"*\n\n| Test | Requirement |\n|------|-------------|\n| `test_single_card_mv4_is_exiled` | A single card with MV=4 satisfies threshold; only that card is exiled |\n| `test_single_card_mv_above_4_is_exiled` | A card with MV>4 satisfies threshold on its own |\n| `test_two_cards_summing_to_mv4_are_both_exiled` | Two cards summing to MV=4 are both exiled; cards beyond threshold are NOT |\n| `test_card_mv_exactly_4_stops_after_one_card` | Exactly MV=4 stops after one card — next card is not touched |\n| `test_zero_mv_cards_all_exiled_when_library_runs_out` | Zero-MV cards never hit the threshold; entire library is exiled if all are zero MV |\n| `test_empty_library_does_not_raise` | Empty library must not throw an exception |\n| `test_mv1_mv1_mv2_all_exiled_at_threshold` | Cards summing exactly to 4 (1+1+2) are all exiled; next card is left in library |\n\n**Edge cases covered:**\n- Threshold reached exactly vs. exceeded\n- Multiple small cards accumulating\n- Library exhaustion without ever reaching threshold\n- Zero-cost cards (MV=0)\n- Cards beyond the threshold remain in library\n\n**Edge cases not covered:**\n- Cards with X in mana cost (engine may treat X as 0 for CMC; ambiguous for this effect)\n- Split cards, double-faced cards (not present in engine model)\n\n---\n\n### Class: `TestImprovisationCapstoneFreecast` (2 tests)\n\nTests the free-cast clause: *\"You may cast any number of spells from among them without paying their mana costs.\"*\n\n| Test | Requirement |\n|------|-------------|\n| `test_exiled_cards_can_be_cast_free` | Exiled cards land in exile zone (prerequisite for free casting) |\n| `test_exiled_cards_have_free_cast_flag_or_equivalent` | Implementation makes exiled cards available for free casting (verifies exile landing) |\n\n**Why limited:** The \"you may cast any number\" clause requires interactive player choice (multiple choose_yes_no and cast_spell_free calls). The engine's DeterministicPlayer doesn't have a scripted multi-cast flow to test the full interaction. The core observable behavior is that exiled cards are in the exile zone and accessible. The full free-cast pipeline is untestable in the current test harness — documented in `untestable.json`.\n\n---\n\n### Class: `TestImprovisationCapstoneParadigmSelfExile` (3 tests)\n\nTests the Paradigm self-exile clause: *\"Then exile this spell.\"*\n\n| Test | Requirement |\n|------|-------------|\n| `test_card_is_not_in_graveyard_after_resolution` | After resolution, the card must not be in the graveyard (Paradigm redirects it to exile) |\n| `test_card_is_in_exile_after_paradigm_resolution` | After resolution, the card is in the exile zone |\n| `test_paradigm_resolved_flag_set_after_first_resolution` | Some indication that Paradigm has fired — flag, player marker, or registered trigger |\n\n**Note:** The test seeds the card in the graveyard before calling `on_resolve` to simulate the engine having moved it there. The implementation is expected to move it to exile during or after `on_resolve`.\n\n---\n\n### Class: `TestImprovisationCapstoneParadigmTrigger` (5 tests)\n\nTests the Paradigm recurring trigger clause: *\"After you first resolve a spell with this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the beginning of each of your first main phases.\"*\n\n| Test | Requirement |\n|------|-------------|\n| `test_paradigm_registers_main_phase_trigger_after_resolve` | Resolving must register at least one new trigger |\n| `test_paradigm_trigger_fires_on_main_phase_event` | The registered trigger must be a `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` trigger |\n| `test_paradigm_trigger_condition_matches_controller` | Trigger condition must match the controller's main phase, not the opponent's |\n| `test_paradigm_trigger_fires_on_controller_main_phase` | Firing the event for the controller pushes a stack object |\n| `test_paradigm_trigger_does_not_fire_for_opponent_main_phase` | Firing the event for the opponent does NOT push a stack object |\n\n**Edge cases covered:**\n- Player identity check (controller vs. opponent)\n- APNAP ordering (implicit via trigger condition)\n\n**Edge cases not covered:**\n- \"First main phase\" restriction (PRECOMBAT_MAIN vs. POSTCOMBAT_MAIN) — the `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` fires for both per KEY_DECISIONS. The per-card implementation may filter on phase; this would require `advance_to_phase` to properly test. Documented in `untestable.json`.\n- The \"copy\" semantics — creating an actual copy of the card vs. the original. This depends on engine support for card copies.\n- \"After you first resolve\" — only the first resolution should register the trigger; subsequent resolutions should not re-register (hard to test without multiple cast cycles).\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n- **22 total test cases** across 5 test classes\n- The tests fail before implementation (TDD red phase) because `ImprovisationCapstone` is a stub with no implementation\n- All assertions test observable behavior: zone contents, trigger counts, trigger conditions\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5348,"cache_read_input_tokens":84019,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5348,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01AGpdidDchSkthiJvVqN48E","session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"7024f8de-02cc-4af8-a129-043e7fdbf8af","request_id":"req_011CbU3epBFwg4nQWnFYEJZu","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Tester for sos_120"}
