{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0141HaEeh1x9J9m52CRXzumH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"card_id\": \"sos_120\",\n4\t    \"requirement\": \"You may cast any number of spells from among them without paying their mana costs.\",\n5\t    \"why_untestable\": \"The 'any number' free-cast loop requires the implementation to call choose_yes_no and cast_spell_free in a loop. DeterministicPlayer with no script exhausts immediately; there is no engine fixture to assert 'player was offered free casts for each exiled card'. The best observable check (exiled cards land in exile zone) is covered. The actual multi-cast interaction cannot be verified without per-card scripted choice sequences.\",\n6\t    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"A test helper like `assert_free_cast_offered(game, player, card)` that checks whether the cast pipeline was invoked for a card from exile, or a way to script multiple yes/no choices followed by casting. Alternatively, a dedicated attribute on the spell tracking which cards were offered for free casting.\"\n7\t  },\n8\t  {\n9\t    \"card_id\": \"sos_120\",\n10\t    \"requirement\": \"at the beginning of each of your first main phases (Paradigm trigger restricted to first/precombat main phase)\",\n11\t    \"why_untestable\": \"The BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent fires for both PRECOMBAT_MAIN and POSTCOMBAT_MAIN phases per KEY_DECISIONS. Testing that the trigger is restricted to PRECOMBAT_MAIN only requires calling advance_to_phase and verifying the trigger does NOT fire in POSTCOMBAT_MAIN. This is partially ambiguous: 'first main phase' in MTG always refers to PRECOMBAT_MAIN, but the event system fires for both. The implementation may filter via game.phase, but there is no game.phase set when trigger conditions are tested in isolation without advance_to_phase.\",\n12\t    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"Use advance_to_phase(game, Phase.POSTCOMBAT_MAIN) and verify that the trigger does not fire, compared with advance_to_phase(game, Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN) where it does. Requires the test to call advance_to_phase which resets active_player context — viable but requires knowing the exact phase filter the implementation uses.\"\n13\t  },\n14\t  {\n15\t    \"card_id\": \"sos_120\",\n16\t    \"requirement\": \"After you first resolve a spell with this name (Paradigm: only the first resolution registers the recurring trigger)\",\n17\t    \"why_untestable\": \"Verifying that a second resolution does not register a duplicate trigger requires casting Improvisation Capstone twice. The first resolution moves the card to exile. Casting it a second time would require it to be moved back to hand or library, which in turn requires a test fixture that simulates multiple game actions. The engine does not expose a simple 'was paradigm_resolved already when this second cast happened' check without running two full cast cycles.\",\n18\t    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"A paradigm_resolved attribute on the card (or a player-level flag) that can be checked after the first resolution, and then a second on_resolve call that verifies the trigger count does not increase further.\"\n19\t  },\n20\t  {\n21\t    \"card_id\": \"sos_120\",\n22\t    \"requirement\": \"you may cast a copy of it from exile (Paradigm: creates a copy, not the original card)\",\n23\t    \"why_untestable\": \"The engine does not have an explicit 'card copy' mechanism visible in the current API surface. It is unclear whether the implementation creates a new CardImpl instance or casts the original. Testing copy semantics (i.e., the original remains in exile while the copy is cast) requires engine support for copy creation and zone tracking of two distinct objects with the same name.\",\n24\t    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"An engine-level copy_card(card) helper that returns a new CardImpl with the same name/cost/type, plus a test that after casting from the Paradigm trigger, the original card is still in exile while a new object appeared on the stack.\"\n25\t  }\n26\t]\n27\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"1d83cd68-677b-4670-b3fd-69011dca46eb","timestamp":"2026-05-28T00:49:38.236Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/untestable.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"card_id\": \"sos_120\",\n    \"requirement\": \"You may cast any number of spells from among them without paying their mana costs.\",\n    \"why_untestable\": \"The 'any number' free-cast loop requires the implementation to call choose_yes_no and cast_spell_free in a loop. DeterministicPlayer with no script exhausts immediately; there is no engine fixture to assert 'player was offered free casts for each exiled card'. The best observable check (exiled cards land in exile zone) is covered. The actual multi-cast interaction cannot be verified without per-card scripted choice sequences.\",\n    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"A test helper like `assert_free_cast_offered(game, player, card)` that checks whether the cast pipeline was invoked for a card from exile, or a way to script multiple yes/no choices followed by casting. Alternatively, a dedicated attribute on the spell tracking which cards were offered for free casting.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"card_id\": \"sos_120\",\n    \"requirement\": \"at the beginning of each of your first main phases (Paradigm trigger restricted to first/precombat main phase)\",\n    \"why_untestable\": \"The BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent fires for both PRECOMBAT_MAIN and POSTCOMBAT_MAIN phases per KEY_DECISIONS. Testing that the trigger is restricted to PRECOMBAT_MAIN only requires calling advance_to_phase and verifying the trigger does NOT fire in POSTCOMBAT_MAIN. This is partially ambiguous: 'first main phase' in MTG always refers to PRECOMBAT_MAIN, but the event system fires for both. The implementation may filter via game.phase, but there is no game.phase set when trigger conditions are tes