{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01SJQjqZAdJJhAswKvNyJ5JD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018nRnuXRnvQ6ddAd27M55cL","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/coordinator-directives.md","content":"# Coordinator Directives for sos_120\n\n## Untestable items — accepted partial coverage\n\nThese 4 items are accepted as partial coverage with markers in the implementation:\n\n1. **Multi-cast free-cast loop**: The implementation should offer free casts for each exiled card, but the exact looping behavior cannot be deterministically tested. Add `# UNVERIFIED: any number of free casts offered` comment.\n\n2. **First main phase restriction for Paradigm trigger**: The Paradigm trigger should only fire at PRECOMBAT_MAIN, not POSTCOMBAT_MAIN. Filter on the event's phase. Add a `paradigm_phase_restriction = \"PRECOMBAT_MAIN\"` attribute for observability.\n\n3. **Paradigm single-registration guard**: Expose a `paradigm_resolved: bool` attribute on the card that is set to True after the first resolution. Use it to guard against duplicate trigger registration.\n\n4. **Copy semantics**: For simplicity, the \"copy\" in the Paradigm trigger can cast the original exiled card (not a true copy), since a full copy mechanism is out of scope. Add `# UNVERIFIED: cast copy vs original` comment.\n\n## Implementation guidance\n\n- The main effect exiles opponent's creatures with MV ≤ 4, controller may cast them for free.\n- The Paradigm effect registers a recurring trigger that fires at the beginning of each PRECOMBAT_MAIN phase to cast a copy of Improvisation Capstone from exile for free.\n- Use BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent (already in engine.events) filtering on PRECOMBAT_MAIN only.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1077,"cache_read_input_tokens":51447,"cache_creation"