{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014t9aYDW9qLrU5f1Jz3GVee","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator Directives for sos_120\n2\t\n3\t## Untestable items — accepted partial coverage\n4\t\n5\tThese 4 items are accepted as partial coverage with markers in the implementation:\n6\t\n7\t1. **Multi-cast free-cast loop**: The implementation should offer free casts for each exiled card, but the exact looping behavior cannot be deterministically tested. Add `# UNVERIFIED: any number of free casts offered` comment.\n8\t\n9\t2. **First main phase restriction for Paradigm trigger**: The Paradigm trigger should only fire at PRECOMBAT_MAIN, not POSTCOMBAT_MAIN. Filter on the event's phase. Add a `paradigm_phase_restriction = \"PRECOMBAT_MAIN\"` attribute for observability.\n10\t\n11\t3. **Paradigm single-registration guard**: Expose a `paradigm_resolved: bool` attribute on the card that is set to True after the first resolution. Use it to guard against duplicate trigger registration.\n12\t\n13\t4. **Copy semantics**: For simplicity, the \"copy\" in the Paradigm trigger can cast the original exiled card (not a true copy), since a full copy mechanism is out of scope. Add `# UNVERIFIED: cast copy vs original` comment.\n14\t\n15\t## Implementation guidance\n16\t\n17\t- The main effect exiles opponent's creatures with MV ≤ 4, controller may cast them for free.\n18\t- The Paradigm effect registers a recurring trigger that fires at the beginning of each PRECOMBAT_MAIN phase to cast a copy of Improvisation Capstone from exile for free.\n19\t- Use BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent (already in engine.events) filtering on PRECOMBAT_MAIN only.\n20\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LW1BNc6CoXS78pX9RyGxVm","session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"5db375cb-6d00-427a-a119-428ddfcd632c","timestamp":"2026-05-28T00:50:11.702Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implementer for sos_120"}
