{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01Gg3zfCfoG5SxtjV1Fc7cyq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N2ABpjkxgGDppSopJ6x7cm","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation Rationale — sos_120 Improvisation Capstone\n\n## Design decisions\n\n### Card base class\nSubclasses `Sorcery` (from `engine.card`) which auto-adds `CardType.SORCERY`. The subtype `{\"Lesson\"}` is set via `kwargs.setdefault(\"subtypes\", {\"Lesson\"})`.\n\n### Main effect (library exile loop)\n`on_resolve` iterates the library top-to-bottom by calling `library.get_all()[-1]` (the last element is the top per `ZoneContainer` convention), removes the card, places it in exile, accumulates its CMC (`mana_cost.cmc`), and stops once the total MV >= 4. If the library empties before reaching 4, the loop terminates naturally without error.\n\n### Free-cast offer (`_offer_free_casts`)\nUses a `try/except` around `choose_yes_no` per the `KEY_DECISIONS.md` convention. Defaults to `False` (no auto-cast) in test contexts where no scripted choice is available, so that exile-state assertions are not perturbed by unexpected card-casting side-effects. A comment marks it as `# UNVERIFIED: any number of free casts offered` per coordinator directive.\n\n### Paradigm self-exile\n`_paradigm_resolve` checks whether `self` is in the owner's graveyard (as placed by the engine after spell resolution) and moves it to exile. If it is not in the graveyard (engine moved it elsewhere) it ensures it is added to exile. This handles both the test scenario (card pre-placed in graveyard) and any engine path that skips the graveyard.\n\n### Paradigm single-registration guard\n`paradigm_resolved: bool` instance attribute is set to `True` before calling `_register_paradigm_trigger`, guarding against duplicate trigger registration on hypothetical second resolutions. This attribute is also tested directly by `test_paradigm_resolved_flag_set_after_first_resolution`.\n\n### Paradigm recurring trigger\n`_register_paradigm_trigger` registers a `TriggerRegistration` for `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` with a condition that checks `event.player is controller`. This ensures the trigger fires only for the controller's main phase (satisfying the opponent-main-phase test). The trigger is NOT one-shot — it stays registered for every subsequent PRECOMBAT_MAIN phase per the Paradigm text. The `paradigm_phase_restriction = \"PRECOMBAT_MAIN\"` class attribute is set for observability per coordinator directive.\n\n### Paradigm free-cast effect (`_paradigm_free_cast`)\nSearches exile for the original card object (or any card named \"Improvisation Capstone\"), asks the player with `choose_yes_no` (defaulting to `True` in test contexts), then calls `cast_spell_free` from exile. Marked `# UNVERIFIED: cast copy vs original` per coordinator directive.\n\n## Deviations from spec\n- The spec says \"cast a copy\" — we cast the original exiled card (no true copy mechanism). Marked as UNVERIFIED per coordinator directive.\n- The Paradigm trigger fires for all subsequent precombat main phases (not just \"first\" in a loop sense), which matches the card oracle text.\n\n## Conventions established\n- Free-cast loops use `try/except` around `choose_yes_no` with `proceed = False` default to avoid side-effects in tests.\n- `paradigm_resolved` instance attribute pattern for cards with Paradigm keyword.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":139,"cache_read_input_tokens":49794,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":139,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":53,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LW1BNc6CoXS78pX9RyGxVm","session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"5d7a9d40-8972-40ce-94a7-8c2a0bc941f3","request_id":"req_011CbU3uBiCqxYCAuNKmWUHr","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implementer for sos_120"}
