{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_011QVMfwbkzvFXF6zqZQZuVk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RjK69eyS5RMcfZpPQ6oz3h","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/review.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 210,\n    \"comment\": \"The Paradigm trigger condition `event.player is controller` cannot distinguish PRECOMBAT_MAIN from POSTCOMBAT_MAIN because `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` has no `phase` attribute. Per KEY_DECISIONS.md, this event fires at BOTH main phases each turn. The card text says 'at the beginning of each of your first main phases' (i.e. PRECOMBAT_MAIN only). Without a phase field on the event, the trigger will fire twice per turn — once at precombat main and once at postcombat main — doubling the number of free-cast offers per turn. The `paradigm_phase_restriction` class attribute documents the intent but is never enforced in the condition. Either the `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` needs a `phase` field and the condition needs to check it, or a separate event must be used for PRECOMBAT_MAIN only.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 127,\n    \"comment\": \"The Paradigm self-exile logic in `_paradigm_resolve` has an incorrect zone assumption. When called from `on_resolve`, the card is still in `Zone.STACK` (the engine moves it to the graveyard AFTER `on_resolve` returns, per `_resolve_spell` in `casting.py`). Because `graveyard.contains(self)` is False and `exile.contains(self)` is also False at this point, the code falls into `exile.add(self)`, placing a copy-reference in exile while the original is still in STACK. After `on_resolve` returns, the engine's `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.GRAVEYARD)` still executes (the card is found in STACK), so the card ends up in both exile AND graveyard simultaneously. The tests side-step this by manually pre-placing the spell in the graveyard before calling `on_resolve`, but a real cast path would be broken. A replacement effect on the zone move (redirecting STACK→GRAVEYARD to STACK→EXILE) would be the correct approach.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 134,\n    \"comment\": \"`paradigm_resolved` is set to `True` on line 134 before the `controller is None` guard on line 136. If `controller` is None on first resolution, the flag is permanently set but the trigger is never registered. Subsequent resolutions with a valid controller will be silently skipped by the guard. Moving the `paradigm_resolved = True` assignment to after the `controller is None` check would fix this logic ordering issue.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 21,\n    \"comment\": \"`CardType` is imported from `engine.types` but is never used in the module body. This is a dead import that should be removed.\"\n  }\n]\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":212,"cache_read_input_tokens":41347,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":212,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":51,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012o3RzbieRBAmQDAudt7ht5","session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"dd750558-39d5-450f-ae38-35f70ab0b05c","request_id":"req_011CbU447fNQvJos6fJQn5km","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Reviewer for sos_120"}
