{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01D9a7EzgNPAkhQwYzn9fXZJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017QnMfWUkmRwc4jTm9XHUXu","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/review.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":968,"cache_read_input_tokens":8533,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":968,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018W5msMc4snNkXsB1RqC4SD","session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"01c5bdb2-b8e0-423e-9b64-178c08674f43","request_id":"req_011CbU46Y28vwARLU4mtSWL3","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revision round for sos_120"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017QnMfWUkmRwc4jTm9XHUXu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n4\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n5\t    \"line\": 210,\n6\t    \"comment\": \"The Paradigm trigger condition `event.player is controller` cannot distinguish PRECOMBAT_MAIN from POSTCOMBAT_MAIN because `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` has no `phase` attribute. Per KEY_DECISIONS.md, this event fires at BOTH main phases each turn. The card text says 'at the beginning of each of your first main phases' (i.e. PRECOMBAT_MAIN only). Without a phase field on the event, the trigger will fire twice per turn — once at precombat main and once at postcombat main — doubling the number of free-cast offers per turn. The `paradigm_phase_restriction` class attribute documents the intent but is never enforced in the condition. Either the `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` needs a `phase` field and the condition needs to check it, or a separate event must be used for PRECOMBAT_MAIN only.\"\n7\t  },\n8\t  {\n9\t    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n10\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n11\t    \"line\": 127,\n12\t    \"comment\": \"The Paradigm self-exile logic in `_paradigm_resolve` has an incorrect zone assumption. When called from `on_resolve`, the card is still in `Zone.STACK` (the engine moves it to the graveyard AFTER `on_resolve` returns, per `_resolve_spell` in `casting.py`). Because `graveyard.contains(self)` is False and `exile.contains(self)` is also False at this point, the code falls into `exile.add(self)`, placing a copy-reference in exile while the original is still in STACK. After `on_resolve` returns, the engine's `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.GRAVEYARD)` still executes (the card is found in STACK), so the card ends up in both exile AND graveyard simultaneously. The tests side-step this by manually pre-placing the spell in the graveyard before calling `on_resolve`, but a real cast path would be broken. A replacement effect on the zone move (redirecting STACK→GRAVEYARD to STACK→EXILE) would be the correct approach.\"\n13\t  },\n14\t  {\n15\t    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n16\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n17\t    \"line\": 134,\n18\t    \"comment\": \"`paradigm_resolved` is set to `True` on line 134 before the `controller is None` guard on line 136. If `controller` is None on first resolution, the flag is permanently set but the trigger is never registered. Subsequent resolutions with a valid controller will be silently skipped by the guard. Moving the `paradigm_resolved = True` assignment to after the `controller is None` check would fix this logic ordering issue.\"\n19\t  },\n20\t  {\n21\t    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n22\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n23\t    \"line\": 21,\n24\t    \"comment\": \"`CardType` is imported from `engine.types` but is never used in the module body. This is a dead import that should be removed.\"\n25\t  }\n26\t]\n27\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018W5msMc4snNkXsB1RqC4SD","session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"22dc6017-4ad7-41ac-abd4-70f2f9bbb2ce","timestamp":"2026-05-28T00:54:15.165Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revision round for sos_120"}
