{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01UttGPcF5nJRxtmUcADRMse","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012A9ER3EaQZLKxYUqeUKooZ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/impl-revised-rationale.md","content":"# Revision Rationale — sos_120 Improvisation Capstone\n\n## Changes Applied\n\n### Strict Comment 0 (line 210): Add `phase` attribute to `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`\n\nAdded a `phase: Any = None` attribute to `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` in `engine/events.py`.\nUpdated `engine/turn.py` to pass `phase=game.phase` when firing the event at both PRECOMBAT_MAIN and POSTCOMBAT_MAIN phase starts.\n\nUpdated the Paradigm trigger condition in `_register_paradigm_trigger` to check:\n```python\nif event.phase is not None and event.phase is not Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN:\n    return False\n```\nThe `phase is not None` guard preserves backwards compatibility with any callers that fire the event without setting a phase (they would still match, per the prior convention that event.player was the sole filter).\n\n### Strict Comment 1 (line 127): Fix the Paradigm self-exile logic\n\nThe reviewer correctly identified that calling `_paradigm_resolve` from `on_resolve` (while the card is still in STACK) would double-place the card in exile and graveyard simultaneously when cast through the real casting pipeline.\n\n**Fix approach**: Added `exile_on_resolve: bool = True` attribute on `ImprovisationCapstone`. Modified `_resolve_spell` in `engine/casting.py` to check for this attribute and route the card to `Zone.EXILE` instead of `Zone.GRAVEYARD` after resolution. This is a clean, additive-only engine change.\n\nFor direct-call test compatibility (tests pre-place the card in graveyard and call `on_resolve` directly), the existing graveyard→exile logic in `_paradigm_resolve` remains. In the real cast path, the card arrives in STACK → `exile_on_resolve` routes it to EXILE → `_paradigm_resolve` finds it neither in graveyard nor exile-yet (since it hasn't moved yet at `on_resolve` call time), but `exile_on_resolve` ensures the engine moves it to exile after `on_resolve` returns, avoiding double-residence.\n\nWait — in the real cast path, `_paradigm_resolve` is called during `on_resolve`, at which point the card is in STACK. The `elif not exile.contains(self)` branch would add it to exile. Then when `on_resolve` returns, `_resolve_spell` sees `exile_on_resolve=True` and calls `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.EXILE)` — but the card is no longer in STACK (it was added to exile during `_paradigm_resolve`). This would cause an `IllegalMoveError`.\n\nTo fix: the `_paradigm_resolve` check should skip adding to exile when the card is still in STACK (i.e., when called from the real cast path). The card being in STACK means `exile_on_resolve` will handle the move after `on_resolve` returns.\n\nActually, looking at the test path: tests pre-place the card in graveyard. In that path the card is in GRAVEYARD when `_paradigm_resolve` runs — the graveyard→exile logic fires correctly. In the real cast path, the card is in STACK — `_paradigm_resolve`'s `elif not exile.contains(self): exile.add(self)` would add it to exile while it's still conceptually in STACK. Then `exile_on_resolve` would try to move from STACK but it's gone.\n\nThe cleanest fix: in `_paradigm_resolve`, only do the manual exile if the card is found in graveyard. If it's found neither in graveyard nor exile, it's being resolved through the pipeline (STACK), and `exile_on_resolve` will handle the move. Updated the code accordingly.\n\n### Advisory Comment 2 (paradigm_resolved ordering): Applied\n\nMoved `self.paradigm_resolved = True` to after the `controller is None` guard. This ensures that if `controller` is None on first resolution, the flag is not set prematurely — a subsequent valid-controller resolution can still register the trigger.\n\n### Advisory Comment 3 (dead import): Applied\n\nRemoved unused `CardType` import from `engine.types`.\n\n## Files Changed\n\n- `engine/events.py`: Added `phase` attribute to `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`\n- `engine/turn.py`: Pass `phase=game.phase` when firing `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`\n- `engine/casting.py`: Added `exile_on_resolve` check in `_resolve_spell` to route Paradigm spells to exile\n- `cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py`: Set `exile_on_resolve=True`, fixed phase filter condition, fixed paradigm_resolved ordering, removed dead `CardType` import, fixed `_paradigm_resolve` to not double-add to exile in the real cast path\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":116,"cache_read_input_tokens":57522,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":116,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":50,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018W5msMc4snNkXsB1RqC4SD","session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"88129e3b-337b-44e6-8b04-3d9f194a3a13","request_id":"req_011CbU4Gk8SDGsP6frXgPGMp","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revision round for sos_120"}
