{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YBKio8mX8ujt2rVieSSc9f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Revision Rationale — sos_120 Improvisation Capstone\n2\t\n3\t## Strict Comment 0 (line 210): Phase filter on BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent\n4\t\n5\tAdded `phase: Any = None` attribute to `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` in `engine/events.py`. The docstring was updated to reflect that the event fires at both PRECOMBAT_MAIN and POSTCOMBAT_MAIN. Updated `engine/turn.py` to pass `phase=game.phase` when firing the event so callers can distinguish the two main phases.\n6\t\n7\tUpdated the Paradigm trigger condition in `_register_paradigm_trigger` to check:\n8\t- `event.player is not controller` → False (same as before)\n9\t- `event.phase is not None and event.phase is not Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN` → False (new guard)\n10\t\n11\tThe `event.phase is not None` check preserves backwards compatibility with legacy callers that fire the event without a phase value.\n12\t\n13\t## Strict Comment 1 (line 127): Paradigm self-exile correctness\n14\t\n15\t**Problem**: When `on_resolve` is called during the real casting pipeline, the card is in `Zone.STACK`. The old `_paradigm_resolve` code's `elif not exile.contains(self): exile.add(self)` would add the card to exile while it was still in STACK. Then `_resolve_spell` would attempt `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`, raising `IllegalMoveError` because the card was already moved out of STACK.\n16\t\n17\t**Fix (two-part)**:\n18\t\n19\t1. Added `exile_on_resolve: bool = True` to `ImprovisationCapstone.__init__`. Modified `_resolve_spell` in `engine/casting.py` with an additive-only `elif getattr(card, \"exile_on_resolve\", False)` branch that routes the card to `Zone.EXILE` instead of `Zone.GRAVEYARD` after resolution. This is the correct replacement-effect-like approach for the real cast path.\n20\t\n21\t2. Fixed `_paradigm_resolve` to detect when the card is still in `Zone.STACK` (real cast path) and skip the manual exile in that case — `exile_on_resolve` handles it after `on_resolve` returns. For the direct-call test path (where tests manually pre-place the card in the graveyard), the existing `graveyard.contains(self)` → remove/add-to-exile logic still fires correctly.\n22\t\n23\tThe three cases now handled:\n24\t- Card in GRAVEYARD (test path, pre-placed): move graveyard → exile immediately\n25\t- Card in STACK (real cast path): do nothing — `exile_on_resolve` moves STACK → EXILE after `on_resolve` returns\n26\t- Card elsewhere: fallback add to exile\n27\t\n28\t## Advisory Comment 2 (paradigm_resolved ordering): Applied\n29\t\n30\tMoved `self.paradigm_resolved = True` to after the `controller is None` guard. If `controller` is None on first resolution, the flag is not prematurely set, allowing a valid subsequent resolution to register the trigger."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"b9e68220-6117-4f47-9bbd-c25287f26b83","timestamp":"2026-05-28T00:58:46.525Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/impl-revised-rationale.md","content":"# Revision Rationale — sos_120 Improvisation Capstone\n\n## Strict Comment 0 (line 210): Phase filter on BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent\n\nAdded `phase: Any = None` attribute to `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` in `engine/events.py`. The docstring was updated to reflect that the event fires at both PRECOMBAT_MAIN and POSTCOMBAT_MAIN. Updated `engine/turn.py` to pass `phase=game.phase` when firing the event so callers can distinguish the two main phases.\n\nUpdated the Paradigm trigger condition in `_register_paradigm_trigger` to check:\n- `event.player is not controller` → False (same as before)\n- `event.phase is not None and event.phase is not Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN` → False (new guard)\n\nThe `event.phase is not None` check preserves backwards compatibility with legacy callers that fire the event without a phase value.\n\n## Strict Comment 1 (line 127): Paradigm self-exile correctness\n\n**Problem**: When `on_resolve` is called during the real casting pipeline, the card is in `Zone.STACK`. The old `_paradigm_resolve` code's `elif not exile.contains(self): exile.add(self)` would add the card to exile while it was still in STACK. Then `_resolve_spell` would attempt `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`, raising `IllegalMoveError` because the card was already moved out of STACK.\n\n**Fix (two-part)**:\n\n1. Added `exile_on_resolve: bool = True` to `ImprovisationCapstone.__init__`. Modified `_resolve_spell` in `engine/casting.py` with an additive-only `elif getattr(card, \"exile_on_resolve\", False)` branch that routes the card to `Zone.EXILE` instead of `Zone.GRAVEYARD` after resolution. This is the correct replacement-effect-like approach for the real cast path.\n\n2. Fixed `_paradigm_resolve` to detect when the card is still in `Zone.STACK` (real cast path) and skip the manual exile in that case — `exile_on_resolve` handles it after `on_resolve` returns. For the direct-call test path (where tests manually pre-place the card in the graveyard), the existing `graveyard.contains(self)` → remove/add-to-exile logic still fires correctly.\n\nThe three cases now handled:\n- Card in GRAVEYARD (test path, pre-placed): move graveyard → exile immediately\n- Card in STACK (real cast path): do nothing — `exile_on_resolve` moves STACK → EXILE after `on_resolve` returns\n- Card elsewhere: fallback add to exile\n\n## Advisory Comment 2 (paradigm_resolved ordering): Applied\n\nMoved `self.paradigm_resolved = True` to after the `controller is None` guard. If `controller` is None on first resolution, the flag is not prematurely set, allowing a valid subsequent resolution to register the trigger.","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":42}}}
