{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_0144tS22N5VTFFpyUej4LchU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NTFaudmNentHFhvQcnjBCX","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale: sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian\n\n## Test File: /workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py\n\nThe card has three functional areas: static properties/keywords, an opponent-upkeep triggered loot ability, and a continuous miracle-granting effect on instants/sorceries in hand.\n\n---\n\n### TestLoreholdStaticProperties\n\n| Test | Requirement validated |\n|------|-----------------------|\n| `test_name` | Card name matches spec exactly. |\n| `test_mana_cost` | Mana cost is `{3}{R}{W}`. |\n| `test_is_creature` | Class inherits from `Creature`; `CardType.CREATURE` in `card_types`. |\n| `test_is_legendary` | `Supertype.LEGENDARY` in supertypes. |\n| `test_subtypes_include_elder_dragon` | Subtypes contain both \"Elder\" and \"Dragon\". |\n| `test_power_is_5` | `base_power == 5`. |\n| `test_toughness_is_5` | `base_toughness == 5`. |\n\n---\n\n### TestLoreholdKeywords\n\n| Test | Requirement validated |\n|------|-----------------------|\n| `test_has_flying` | `Keyword.FLYING` in `keywords`. |\n| `test_has_haste` | `Keyword.HASTE` in `keywords`. |\n\n---\n\n### TestLoreholdUpkeepTriggerRegistration\n\n| Test | Requirement validated |\n|------|-----------------------|\n| `test_registers_at_least_one_trigger` | `register_triggers` adds at least one entry to the trigger manager. |\n| `test_registers_upkeep_trigger_type` | The registered trigger uses `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` as its event type. |\n| `test_unregister_removes_triggers` | After `trigger_manager.unregister(card)`, no triggers from this source remain. |\n\n---\n\n### TestLoreholdUpkeepTriggerCondition\n\n| Test | Requirement validated |\n|------|-----------------------|\n| `test_trigger_fires_on_opponent_upkeep` | When the active player is the opponent (player index 1) and an upkeep event fires, the stack grows — the trigger correctly fires on the opponent's upkeep. |\n| `test_trigger_does_not_fire_on_controller_upkeep` | When the active player is the controller (player index 0), the stack does not grow — the trigger must NOT fire on the controller's own upkeep. The test now also verifies the trigger IS registered (precondition) to avoid a vacuous pass. |\n\n**Why only these cases**: The card says \"each opponent's upkeep\". In a two-player game there is exactly one opponent, so the two cases are exhaustive. Multi-opponent scenarios are out of scope for a two-player engine.\n\n---\n\n### TestLoreholdUpkeepTriggerEffect\n\n| Test | Requirement validated |\n|------|-----------------------|\n| `test_discard_yes_removes_card_from_hand` | Choosing yes: the chosen card leaves the hand and lands in the graveyard. |\n| `test_discard_yes_draws_a_card` | Choosing yes: a new card is drawn from the library into the hand. |\n| `test_discard_no_does_not_discard_or_draw` | Choosing no: hand size and library size are both unchanged. |\n| `test_discard_yes_empty_hand_skips_draw` | Edge case: when the hand is empty the trigger either does not fire or handles the no-card-to-discard state gracefully without crashing. |\n\n**Edge cases not covered**:\n- Drawing from an empty library when discarding was chosen: the engine already handles this via `drawn_from_empty_library` flag and is tested in engine_tests — not duplicated here.\n- Exactly which card is discarded when multiple cards are present: the player's `choose_card` is responsible; we script it and verify the scripted card is discarded.\n\n---\n\n### TestLoreholdMiracleGrant\n\n| Test | Requirement validated |\n|------|-----------------------|\n| `test_instant_in_hand_has_miracle_cost_attribute` | An `Instant` in the controller's hand gains `miracle_cost == ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\")`. |\n| `test_sorcery_in_hand_has_miracle_cost_attribute` | A `Sorcery` in the controller's hand gains `miracle_cost == ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\")`. |\n| `test_creature_in_hand_does_not_get_miracle` | A `Creature` in the controller's hand must NOT have `miracle_cost` set to `{2}` by Lorehold. |\n| `test_miracle_cost_is_exactly_two_generic` | The granted miracle cost parses equal to `ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\")` (two generic mana, no colored pips). |\n\n**How miracle is tested**: The engine has no first-class `miracle` mechanic. The card's implementation is expected to expose the granted miracle cost on each eligible card as a `miracle_cost` attribute (following the pattern used in other cards that expose cost-reduction attributes). The test verifies the attribute is set by `register_triggers` and has the correct value. The full cast-for-miracle-cost workflow (drawing as the first card + casting at reduced cost) cannot be fully end-to-end tested with the current engine surface area and is recorded in `untestable.json`.\n\n**Why opponent's cards are not tested**: The oracle text says \"in your hand\", meaning the controller's hand only. No test is needed for the opponent's hand cards.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1153,"cache_read_input_tokens":72638,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1153,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_017TsEYYuWteGB8XGJB5RX3U","session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"5f39d332-1485-4dc1-ba8a-c118920f5d1e","request_id":"req_011CbU4i9yqHZcVjty2jtqtk","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Tester for sos_201"}
