{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01BdhA6be8r19phQUJe1iEdi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014nb9tDZNrbm6y7i5Vuzojh","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/review.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 109,\n    \"comment\": \"_remove_miracle_hook() is defined but never called. The engine's move_to_zone only calls game.trigger_manager.unregister(card) and game.replacement_manager.unregister(card) when Lorehold leaves the battlefield — it does not invoke any custom cleanup method on the card object. As a result, the monkey-patch on hand.add persists permanently after Lorehold leaves the battlefield, and future instants/sorceries added to the controller's hand will continue receiving miracle_cost={2} even when Lorehold is no longer on the battlefield. A LeavesBattlefieldTriggeredEvent trigger registered in register_triggers() that calls self._remove_miracle_hook() would fix this.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 98,\n    \"comment\": \"The _patched_add closure contains the comment 'If Lorehold is still on the battlefield (or at least registered)' but performs no such check. The variable `source = self` captured at line 94 is never referenced inside the closure body, so the hook always fires unconditionally regardless of whether Lorehold is on the battlefield. The closure should check e.g. `if source._hooked_hand_zone is not None` or use some zone-membership check before granting miracle_cost, so that the effect stops applying once Lorehold has left.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 94,\n    \"comment\": \"The variable `source = self` is assigned to capture `self` for the closure but is never referenced in the closure body (_pat