{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MNtMDsq6iBBUguZheEEhiX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator Directives for sos_226\n2\t\n3\t## Untestable item: copy spell and choose new targets\n4\tThe casualty effect copies the spell. To make this testable, the implementation should expose `self._last_copy` attribute (the StackObject of the most recently created copy) after executing the copy. This allows tests to inspect the copy's targets separately from the original.\n5\t\n6\tImplement the copy effect and store the resulting StackObject in `self._last_copy = copy_stack_obj`. The \"choose new targets\" part can use try/except fallback pattern (per KEY_DECISIONS.md) since DeterministicPlayer may not have scripted choices.\n7\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JVqNS9Hqi2uvrE94ipz5bt","session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"1b709842-4d91-4cf0-9f8a-fc7931e98425","timestamp":"2026-05-28T01:14:56.205Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implementer for sos_226"}
