{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01Dt7QnJqBjhYGha544LPg8T","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AJSM5ngqWwxNNrM4Ky3U7i","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation Rationale — sos_226 Silverquill, the Disputant\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### Card Structure\n`SilverquillTheDisputant` extends `Creature` directly. It sets `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtypes `{\"Elder\", \"Dragon\"}`, and keywords `FLYING | VIGILANCE` in `__init__`. The `base_power=4` and `base_toughness=4` are passed via `kwargs.setdefault`.\n\n### Trigger Registration\nThe casualty mechanic is implemented as a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger registered in `register_triggers`. This matches the fdn_92 (Rite of the Dragoncaller) pattern, which also watches `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` for instant/sorcery filtering.\n\n### Condition Logic\nThe condition checks:\n1. The caster matches the controller (not opponent's spells)\n2. The spell's card_types contain INSTANT or SORCERY\n\nThis satisfies the test requirement that `trigger.condition` returns `False` for creatures/enchantments and opponent-cast spells.\n\n### Effect Logic (Casualty)\nThe effect (called as `trigger.effect(game)` in tests):\n1. Asks `choose_yes_no` for casualty sacrifice — returns False immediately if declined\n2. Finds legal victims: creatures on controller's battlefield with `power >= 1`\n3. Returns without copy if no legal victims (handles power-0 case)\n4. Asks `choose_card` to pick a victim\n5. Validates victim's power >= 1 (defense against invalid choice)\n6. Sacrifices by removing from battlefield and adding to graveyard\n7. Searches stack from top for an instant/sorcery StackObject by controller\n8. Calls `copy_spell(game, original_so, ctrl, new_targets)` and pushes the copy\n9. Stores the copy in `self._last_copy` (per coordinator directives)\n\n### Stack Search Pattern\nRather than the Thousand-Year Storm approach (storing `_pending_spell` in the condition), the effect searches `game.stack._items` in reverse for a StackObject whose source is an instant/sorcery. This works for the test pattern where `trigger.effect(game)` is called directly (bypassing `_condition`). If `_condition` is used normally, the spell will be on the stack as pushed during casting.\n\n### try/except Fallbacks\nPer `KEY_DECISIONS.md`, all `choose_yes_no`/`choose_card`/`choose_target` calls in trigger effects are wrapped in try/except to handle `ScriptExhaustedError` from `DeterministicPlayer` in test contexts.\n\n### `_last_copy` Attribute\nPer coordinator directives, `self._last_copy` is set to the newly created `StackObject` copy after a successful casualty. Initialized to `None` in `__init__`.\n\n## No Engine Changes\nNo engine files were modified — all logic is self-contained in `card_impl.py`.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":119,"cache_read_input_tokens":55080,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":119,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":48,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JVqNS9Hqi2uvrE94ipz5bt","session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"23a4b5cd-226a-49cf-becc-64cf96263951","request_id":"req_011CbU5qTrBUKWts25suu3E8","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implementer for sos_226"}
