{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01T15ZiVg4A1B8zhKQqHzz82","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016cU8kui3hyUdijzJVJCTjc","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale — SOS 245: Witherbloom, the Balancer\n\n## Card Summary\n\nWitherbloom, the Balancer is a `{6}{B}{G}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon (5/5) with three abilities:\n\n1. **Affinity for creatures (self)**: This spell costs `{1}` less to cast for each creature you control.\n2. **Flying and Deathtouch**: Static keywords.\n3. **Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures**: A static continuous ability granting cost reduction to instants and sorceries the controller casts.\n\n---\n\n## Test File\n\n`/workspace/cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py`\n\n---\n\n## Test Groups\n\n### `TestWitherbloomProperties` (11 tests)\n\nThese tests verify the static card characteristics match the spec exactly:\n- `test_is_creature`: Card is a `Creature` subclass.\n- `test_name`: Name matches \"Witherbloom, the Balancer\".\n- `test_mana_cost`: Mana cost is `{6}{B}{G}`.\n- `test_base_power` / `test_base_toughness`: P/T is 5/5.\n- `test_has_flying` / `test_has_deathtouch`: Both keywords present.\n- `test_is_legendary`: `Supertype.LEGENDARY` in supertypes.\n- `test_creature_card_type`: `CardType.CREATURE` in card_types.\n- `test_elder_subtype` / `test_dragon_subtype`: Subtypes \"Elder\" and \"Dragon\" present.\n\n---\n\n### `TestWitherbloomSelfAffinityCostReduction` (8 tests)\n\nThese tests verify Witherbloom's own `cost_reduction()` method (affinity for creatures applied when Witherbloom itself is being cast):\n\n- `test_no_creatures_no_reduction`: Empty battlefield → 0 reduction. Required because affinity returns 0 when there are no creatures.\n- `test_one_creature_reduces_by_one`: 1 creature → reduction of 1. Basic affinity check.\n- `test_three_creatures_reduces_by_three`: 3 creatures → reduction of 3. Verifies linear scaling.\n- `test_six_creatures_reduces_at_most_six`: 6 creatures → reduction of exactly 6 (fully reduces the {6} generic component).\n- `test_more_than_six_creatures_capped_at_six`: 10 creatures → reduction ≤ 6 (cannot reduce below 0 or below colored costs). Generic portion is 6, so the cap is 6.\n- `test_non_creature_permanents_do_not_count`: Lands and enchantments don't count. Affinity says \"each creature,\" not \"each permanent.\"\n- `test_opponent_creatures_do_not_count`: Only controller's creatures count, not the opponent's.\n- `test_integration_cast_with_six_creatures_pays_only_color`: Integration test — with 6 creatures on board and only `{B}{G}` mana available, casting should succeed because the {6} generic is fully reduced.\n\n---\n\n### `TestWitherbloomAffinityGrantRegistration` (5 tests)\n\nThese tests verify that `register_triggers()` wires the mechanism for granting affinity to instants/sorceries:\n\n- `test_no_triggers_before_register_triggers`: No triggers for this card exist until `register_triggers()` is called.\n- `test_registers_at_least_one_trigger`: At least one trigger is registered after calling `register_triggers()`.\n- `test_registers_spell_cast_triggered_event`: The registered trigger uses `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` (the standard pattern in this codebase for reacting to spell casts).\n- `test_trigger_source_is_witherbloom_instance`: The trigger's source is this specific card instance.\n- `test_trigger_can_be_unregistered`: Calling `game.trigger_manager.unregister(card)` removes all triggers for the card.\n\n**Note**: These tests are implementation-style in that they verify a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger exists. If the implementer uses a completely different mechanism (e.g., a continuous effect or game-state hook), the coordinator may need to dispute these tests. The two integration tests in `TestWitherbloomAffinityGrantEffect` capture the observable behavior regardless of mechanism.\n\n---\n\n### `TestWitherbloomAffinityGrantCondition` (6 tests)\n\nThese tests check the condition logic of the `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger:\n\n- `test_condition_true_for_controller_instant`: An instant cast by the controller triggers the affinity grant.\n- `test_condition_true_for_controller_sorcery`: A sorcery cast by the controller triggers the affinity grant.\n- `test_condition_false_for_controller_creature`: Creatures do NOT trigger the affinity grant (card text says \"instant and sorcery spells\").\n- `test_condition_false_for_controller_enchantment`: Enchantments do NOT trigger.\n- `test_condition_false_for_opponent_instant`: Opponent's instants do NOT trigger (card text says \"you cast\").\n- `test_condition_false_for_opponent_sorcery`: Opponent's sorceries do NOT trigger.\n\nTests with `trigger.condition is None` use `pytest.skip` to avoid false positives (a `None` condition always fires), consistent with the pattern in `sos_226/tests.py`.\n\n---\n\n### `TestWitherbloomAffinityGrantEffect` (4 tests)\n\nThese tests verify the effect of the affinity grant:\n\n- `test_effect_fires_without_error_with_no_creatures`: Effect resolves without error when there are no creatures. Guards against crashes in the 0-creature edge case.\n- `test_effect_fires_without_error_with_creatures`: Effect resolves without error with 3 creatures on the battlefield.\n- `test_instant_cast_cheaper_with_witherbloom_and_creatures`: **Key integration test** — with Witherbloom + 3 bears on battlefield, a `{3}` instant can be cast with zero mana (4 total creatures reduces the cost by 3 or more, making the {3} instant free). Tests the observable behavior of the affinity grant.\n- `test_sorcery_cast_cheaper_with_witherbloom_and_creatures`: **Key integration test** — with Witherbloom + 4 bears on battlefield, a `{4}` sorcery can be cast with zero mana (5 total creatures reduces the cost by 4 or more).\n\n---\n\n## Edge Cases Covered\n\n- Reduction capped at generic mana (cannot over-reduce past colored pips).\n- Opponent's creatures don't count.\n- Non-creature permanents don't count.\n- Witherbloom itself counts as a creature when granting affinity to instants/sorceries (it's on the battlefield).\n- Zero-creature edge case handled gracefully.\n\n## Edge Cases NOT Covered\n\n- **Witherbloom counting itself during its own casting**: When Witherbloom is being cast (from hand), it's not yet on the battlefield, so it shouldn't count itself. This is handled by the engine's casting pipeline setting `card.controller` before calling `cost_reduction`, but we don't explicitly test that Witherbloom excludes itself during its own cast cost calculation. This is implicitly validated by the integration test (6 creatures in battlefield are needed to get {B}{G} cost, showing Witherbloom doesn't pre-count itself).\n- **Interaction with other cost reduction effects**: Not tested — out of scope for this card's requirements.\n- **Tokens as creatures for affinity counting**: Token creatures should count but not explicitly tested; the existing `Creature` objects used suffice.\n- **The \"affinity for creatures\" keyword on instants/sorceries in zones other than the stack**: Not relevant to the engine's implementation.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":507,"cache_read_input_tokens":96224,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":507,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MbHyaV3mBN3p5mAu9EnCqi","session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"4050a74b-e006-438d-99dd-1a5a8cd6cbf6","request_id":"req_011CbU6PphSyrkrZjtaYsSDm","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Tester for sos_245"}
