{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01176dzvb2vUxufEeA97k5cC","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/coordinator-directives.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"0e7112ec-22b1-49f9-9843-4cf17550cc21","timestamp":"2026-05-28T01:27:02.249Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/coordinator-directives.md","content":"# Coordinator Directives for sos_245\n\n## Untestable item: Affinity for creatures on instants/sorceries\nThe tests include integration tests that verify instants/sorceries cost less with Witherbloom + creatures.\n\nThe Implementer needs to add a mechanism to inject cost reduction for spells being cast. Recommended approach:\n- Add a `game.active_cost_reducers` list (or similar global hook) in the game state.\n- When Witherbloom is on the battlefield (via register_triggers or register_replacement_effects), add a reducer entry: {\"condition\": lambda card: instant_or_sorcery, \"reduction\": lambda game: count_creatures(controller)}.\n- Modify `casting.py` (or `card.cost_reduction`) to consult `game.active_cost_reducers` when computing effective cost.\n- Or alternatively: override a `pre_cast_hook` on the game that modifies the spell's cost_reduction during casting.\n\nThe simplest approach: have Witherbloom register a permanent attribute `affinity_grants_active = True` and patch each instant/sorcery spell's `cost_reduction` before they go on the stack. But this requires hooking into the casting pipeline.\n\nLog the chosen mechanism in KEY_DECISIONS.md.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
