{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0165C4rMrZduNZahow3q26Ek","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator Directives for sos_245\n2\t\n3\t## Untestable item: Affinity for creatures on instants/sorceries\n4\tThe tests include integration tests that verify instants/sorceries cost less with Witherbloom + creatures.\n5\t\n6\tThe Implementer needs to add a mechanism to inject cost reduction for spells being cast. Recommended approach:\n7\t- Add a `game.active_cost_reducers` list (or similar global hook) in the game state.\n8\t- When Witherbloom is on the battlefield (via register_triggers or register_replacement_effects), add a reducer entry: {\"condition\": lambda card: instant_or_sorcery, \"reduction\": lambda game: count_creatures(controller)}.\n9\t- Modify `casting.py` (or `card.cost_reduction`) to consult `game.active_cost_reducers` when computing effective cost.\n10\t- Or alternatively: override a `pre_cast_hook` on the game that modifies the spell's cost_reduction during casting.\n11\t\n12\tThe simplest approach: have Witherbloom register a permanent attribute `affinity_grants_active = True` and patch each instant/sorcery spell's `cost_reduction` before they go on the stack. But this requires hooking into the casting pipeline.\n13\t\n14\tLog the chosen mechanism in KEY_DECISIONS.md.\n15\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018LRkPu3v1xUbdH5FNBbAr1","session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"a8e4ad5c-0b28-4790-8d93-fb4b6291b215","timestamp":"2026-05-28T01:27:19.774Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implementer for sos_245"}
