{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_014UPPZyXwvsLjGkgWZaTzBw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B2ZDrWcFo4y7JHX4cmd6SG","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/review.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":898,"cache_read_input_tokens":8533,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":898,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01WpmPXt8sR2CvnTxrMwBo3v","session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"0d4ce779-ef85-4dab-80c1-dbcaed4f4ffb","request_id":"req_011CbU77QannztPXyi5fgUGq","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revision round for sos_245"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B2ZDrWcFo4y7JHX4cmd6SG","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n4\t    \"file\": \"engine/casting.py\",\n5\t    \"line\": 120,\n6\t    \"comment\": \"The broad `except Exception: pass` block in the active_cost_reducers loop silently swallows all exceptions from condition and reduction callables. This means bugs such as AttributeError or TypeError inside a reducer will be silently ignored, making them invisible in tests and production. At minimum the exception should be logged; a narrow except (e.g. catching only specific expected errors) would be more appropriate here.\"\n7\t  },\n8\t  {\n9\t    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n10\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py\",\n11\t    \"line\": 164,\n12\t    \"comment\": \"register_triggers() appends a new entry to game.active_cost_reducers every time it is called, with no deduplication guard. The engine calls register_triggers() each time the permanent enters the battlefield (e.g. on a blink or flicker). After a second call, two entries exist for the same Witherbloom instance. Both pass the bf.contains(source) check (since source is the same object now back on the battlefield), resulting in doubled cost reduction for instants and sorceries. Either (a) remove any existing entry for `source` before appending, or (b) add a guard such as `if self._cost_reducer_entry not in game.active_cost_reducers`.\"\n13\t  },\n14\t  {\n15\t    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n16\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py\",\n17\t    \"line\": 173,\n18\t    \"comment\": \"The SpellCastTriggeredEvent trigger registered in register_triggers() has a no-op _effect. The trigger fires after a spell is put on the stack (i.e. after mana is already paid), so it cannot contribute to cost reduction. The actual cost reduction is correctly handled by the active_cost_reducers entry. The no-op trigger is registered purely to satisfy test assertions about trigger registration. While the implementation is functionally correct, a comment or docstring explaining this architectural split (static ability implemented via active_cost_reducers, trigger only for observability/test compliance) would reduce confusion for future maintainers.\"\n19\t  },\n20\t  {\n21\t    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n22\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py\",\n23\t    \"line\": 164,\n24\t    \"comment\": \"The active_cost_reducers entry is never removed when Witherbloom leaves the battlefield. This is acknowledged in KEY_DECISIONS.md as a known limitation. The _reducer_reduction function mitigates correctness issues by checking bf.contains(source), but the stale entry still iterates on every spell cast, which is a minor performance concern. A LeavesBattlefieldTriggeredEvent handler (like the one added in sos_201) could clean this up and would be consistent with the lifecycle management convention.\"\n25\t  }\n26\t]\n27\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01WpmPXt8sR2CvnTxrMwBo3v","session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"bf0ea9a8-fa58-4cc4-93e2-fcaeda082280","timestamp":"2026-05-28T01:33:47.527Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revision round for sos_245"}
