{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_017n4rEoJiSGeVWxSDvgDPMP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EKUJBdnVcwXfw2SQUE6Axy","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl-revised-rationale.md","content":"# Revision Rationale for sos_245 (Witherbloom, the Balancer)\n\n## Strict comment 0: Narrowed exception handling in engine/casting.py\n\nThe broad `except Exception: pass` in the `get_cost_reduction` loop was replaced\nwith two separate try/except blocks, each catching only `(AttributeError, TypeError)`.\nThese are the only expected failure modes when invoking a malformed or missing\ncallable from a reducer dict entry. Unexpected exceptions (e.g. logic errors,\nNameError inside a reducer body) now propagate normally, making bugs visible in\ntests and production.\n\nThe condition check and the reduction call are now in separate try/except blocks\nso that a failure in the condition does not mask a valid reduction, and vice versa.\n\n## Strict comment 1: Deduplication of active_cost_reducers on re-entry\n\n`register_triggers` now removes any existing entry for `self` from\n`game.active_cost_reducers` before appending the new entry:\n\n```python\ngame.active_cost_reducers[:] = [\n    e for e in game.active_cost_reducers if e.get(\"source\") is not source\n]\ngame.active_cost_reducers.append(reducer_entry)\n```\n\nThis prevents doubled cost reductions after a blink or flicker, where\n`register_triggers` is called a second time for the same object instance.\n\n## Advisory comment 3: LTB cleanup (implemented)\n\nAdded a `LeavesBattlefieldTriggeredEvent` trigger that removes the\n`active_cost_reducers` entry when Witherbloom leaves the battlefield. This is\nconsistent with the lifecycle management convention established in sos_201 and\neliminates the stale-entry iteration concern on every subsequent spell cast.\nThe trigger is registered alongside the existing `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger\nin `register_triggers`, so `trigger_manager.unregister(source)` removes it too.\n\n## Advisory comment 2: No change\n\nThe advisory note about adding a docstring explaining the SpellCastTriggeredEvent /\nactive_cost_reducers architectural split was acknowledged but not actioned as a\ncode change; the existing inline comments already explain the pattern.\n\n## Tests\n\nAll 30 tests for sos_245 continue to pass. The full suite (1428 tests) also passes.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":132,"cache_read_input_tokens":37792,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":132,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":55,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01WpmPXt8sR2CvnTxrMwBo3v","session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"9f1c7e73-53e5-4b21-9b3e-eaa858a68a19","request_id":"req_011CbU7BZRi7fuup8goMJgiz","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revision round for sos_245"}
