{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P9ebWDrXCAW3hF9X87SNwQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"card_id\": \"sos_257\",\n4\t    \"requirement\": \"{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell.\",\n5\t    \"why_untestable\": \"The 'Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell' restriction requires per-mana-unit spending tags in the ManaPool. The engine's ManaPool tracks quantity by type but does not attach conditional spending restrictions to individual mana units, so this restriction cannot be asserted via any public API.\",\n6\t    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"The engine would need a conditional-mana tagging system (e.g. ManaPool.add(..., restriction=<callable>) and enforcement in casting.py's cost-payment path) for this restriction to be testable.\"\n7\t  },\n8\t  {\n9\t    \"card_id\": \"sos_257\",\n10\t    \"requirement\": \"This creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn (end-of-turn cleanup of the power boost).\",\n11\t    \"why_untestable\": \"Verifying that the +1/+0 boost is removed at end of turn requires advancing the game through cleanup and re-reading modified_power, which involves the engine's DURATION_END_OF_TURN continuous-effect expiry and the full turn-advance loop. The per-card test infrastructure (no advance_to_phase call for cleanup, and the effect manager integration) makes this untestable in a targeted unit test without a full turn cycle.\",\n12\t    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"An advance_to_phase(game, Phase.ENDING, Step.CLEANUP) helper that also triggers effect_manager cleanup would allow asserting that modified_power returns to its pre-boost value after the turn ends.\"\n13\t  }\n14\t]\n15\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"e748fadc-fc05-476b-9b4a-070d054cde0f","timestamp":"2026-05-28T01:39:51.139Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordina