{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01DFovPGhC9yP2KfEx3dKigp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WQ5vBWRwichtTTy8bpxvwi","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/review.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":554,"cache_read_input_tokens":77656,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":554},"output_tokens":58,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"14c1777b-c765-417a-b113-5e295ddd42e4","request_id":"req_011CbU85VupsG2MvB5SDXQRa"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WQ5vBWRwichtTTy8bpxvwi","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n4\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py\",\n5\t    \"line\": 180,\n6\t    \"comment\": \"The trigger condition `_condition` does not check `CardType.CREATURE in source.card_types`. Per the spec, the '+1/+0 whenever you cast an instant or sorcery' triggered ability is granted only when this land is a creature (after the {5} animation). Because `register_triggers` is called at ETB (before any animation occurs), the trigger is registered while the land is a plain land. Without a creature-mode guard, the condition returns True for controller instants/sorceries even when the land hasn't been animated, causing `modified_power` to be spuriously incremented on a non-creature land. Fix: add `if CardType.CREATURE not in source.card_types: return False` at the start of `_condition`.\"\n7\t  },\n8\t  {\n9\t    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n10\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py\",\n11\t    \"line\": 104,\n12\t    \"comment\": \"The `_effect_colored` function hardcodes `ManaType.BLUE` instead of producing 'one mana of any color' as the spec requires. The spec text is '{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color.' Hardcoding blue means a player cannot choose white, black, red, or green, which misrepresents the card's mana production. If the engine lacks a `choose_mana_type` API, a reasonable workaround would be to add all five colors each with amount 1 and let the player pick which to spend (common engine pattern), or at minimum document the chosen default and why. As-is, the ability silently produces only blue mana, a strict intent mismatch.\"\n13\t  },\n14\t  {\n15\t    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n16\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py\",\n17\t    \"line\": 143,\n18\t    \"comment\": \"The `_animation_effect` permanently adds `CardType.CREATURE` to `source.card_types` and sets `modified_power`/`modified_toughness` but never schedules an end-of-turn cleanup. The spec says 'becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature... until end of turn.' Without a cleanup hook registered on `EndOfTurnTriggeredEvent` (or `EndStepTriggeredEvent`), the land remains a creature permanently once animated. The comment 'UNVERIFIED: end-of-turn +1/+0 expiry' conflates two separate expiry requirements: (1) the animation itself reverts at EOT, and (2) the +1/+0 bonus expires at EOT. Neither is implemented. Since `EndOfTurnTriggeredEvent` exists in the engine, the animation reversion at minimum should be scheduled.\"\n19\t  },\n20\t  {\n21\t    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n22\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py\",\n23\t    \"line\": 169,\n24\t    \"comment\": \"The docstring for `register_triggers` says 'Register the Wizard trigger if the card is in creature mode.' but the method does not enforce this condition — it always registers the trigger regardless of creature mode. The docstring is misleading. Either update the docstring to reflect that the trigger is registered unconditionally (relying on `_condition` to guard) or add the creature-mode check at registration time. Either way, the missing creature-mode guard in `_condition` (see strict comment above) is the root issue.\"\n25\t  },\n26\t  {\n27\t    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n28\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py\",\n29\t    \"line\": 207,\n30\t    \"comment\": \"The `_effect` of the Wizard trigger increments `source.modified_power` directly without checking whether the land is currently in creature mode. If the creature-mode guard is added to `_condition` (fixing the strict issue), this becomes unreachable in non-creature mode. However, defensive code such as `if CardType.CREATURE not in source.card_types: return` in `_effect` would be safer to prevent inadvertent power modification if the condition is bypassed or called directly in tests.\"\n31\t  }\n32\t]\n33\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc7916e9-61b8-4183-92a0-8e53a58e330b","uuid":"5fb39bcf-4b5b-4a4f-8955-9504d136eec4","timestamp":"2026-05-28T01:46:27.814Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/review.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 180,\n    \"comment\": \"The trigger condition `_condition` does not check `CardType.CREATURE in source.card_types`. Per the spec, the '+1/+0 whenever you cast an instant or sorcery' triggered ability is granted only when this land is a creature (after the {5} animation). Because `register_triggers` is called at ETB (before any animation occurs), the trigger is registered while the land is a plain land. Without a creature-mode guard, the condition returns True for controller instants/sorceries even when the land hasn't been animated, causing `modified_power` to be spuriously incremented on a non-creature land. Fix: add `if CardType.CREATURE not in source.card_types: return False` at the start of `_condition`.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 104,\n    \"comment\": \"The `_effect_colored` function hardcodes `ManaType.BLUE` instead of producing 'one mana of any color' as the spec requires. The spec text is '{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color.' Hardcoding blue means a player cannot choose white, black, red, or green, which misrepresents the card's mana production. If the engine lacks a `choose_mana_type` API, a reasonable workaround would be to add all five colors each with amount 1 and let the player pick which to spend (common engine pattern), or at minimum document the chosen default and why. As-is, the ability silently produces only blue mana, a strict intent mismatch.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 143,\n    \"comment\": \"The `_animation_effect` permanently adds `CardType.CREATURE` to `source.card_types` and sets `modified_power`/`modified_toughness` but never schedules an end-of-turn cleanup. The spec says 'becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature... until end of turn.' Without a cleanup hook registered on `EndOfTurnTriggeredEvent` (or `EndStepTriggeredEvent`), the land remains a creature permanently once animated. The comment 'UNVERIFIED: end-of-turn +1/+0 expiry' conflates two separate expiry requirements: (1) the animation itself reverts at EOT, and (2) the +1/+0 bonus expires at EOT. Neither is implemented. Since `EndOfTurnTriggeredEvent` exists in the engine, the animation reversion at minimum should be scheduled.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 169,\n    \"comment\": \"The docstring for `register_triggers` says 'Register the Wizard trigger if the card is in creature mode.' but the method does not enforce this condition — it always registers the trigger regardless of creature mode. The docstring is misleading. Either update the docstring to reflect that the trigger is registered unconditionally (relying on `_condition` to guard) or add the creature-mode check at registration time. Either way, the missing creature-mode guard in `_condition` (see strict comment above) is the root issue.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 207,\n    \"comment\": \"The `_effect` of the Wizard trigger increments `source.modified_power` directly without checking whether the land is currently in creature mode. If the creature-mode guard is added to `_condition` (fixing the strict issue), this becomes unreachable in non-creature mode. However, defensive code such as `if CardType.CREATURE not in source.card_types: return` in `_effect` would be safer to prevent inadvertent power modification if the condition is bypassed or called directly in tests.\"\n  }\n]\n","numLines":33,"startLine":1,"totalLines":33}}}
